-- Seed Batch 3 lore (missing Beyonders audit): city-level named Beyonders
-- (city-keyed, NOT pathway-keyed per the leak rule) + a Sequence 1-2 angel
-- cleanup (pathway-keyed) that Batch 1 missed. Generated from the canonical
-- TS source (src/lib/lore/npcs.ts). narratorOnly is a TS-only prompt flag
-- (no column), not persisted. Array columns seed as '{}' (never null).

insert into public.lore_entries (slug, title, category, content, pathway, epoch, city, npcs, sequences, tags, token_count)
values
  ('npc-hisoka', 'Hisoka — Desire Apostle of West Balam', 'npc', 'Twanaku Tupián, known by the codename Hisoka, was a transmigrator who seized the body of a West Balam native and remade himself into a Sequence 5 Desire Apostle of the Abyss Pathway, supplemented by a Chained Pathway boon granting him Wraith-level abilities from Naboredisley. Operating out of Tizamo Town and Port Pylos in Matani, he served the Patrol Team publicly and posed as a member of the Church of the Fool''s Rose School of Thought Temperance Faction, while secretly funnelling prayers to the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth — a scheme to help that deity steal the Fool''s identity and divine portfolio.

A methodical hunter, Hisoka craved killing high-potential Beyonders, mirroring the fictional character whose name he borrowed. He held a seventy-thousand-verl-pound bounty for serial murders committed as part of his acting method. He spent years maneuvering to trap Lumian Lee in Port Pylos — relying on intelligence from Loki and the Nois Family''s demon — but Lumian''s companions neutralised him through teamwork. His main body was killed in early December 1358 by Lumian''s blazing-white flaming sword; his dream projection, persisting through Tizamo''s Dream Festival, was destroyed in mid-December 1358.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Hisoka', 'Lumian Lee', 'Loki', 'Hela', 'Franca Roland', 'Anthony Reid', 'Mad Lady', 'Naboredisley', 'Camus Castiya'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['balam', 'west-balam', 'abyss-pathway', 'chained-pathway', 'transmigrator', 'april-fools', 'patrol-team', 'rose-school-of-thought', 'church-of-the-fool', 'serial-killer', 'desire-apostle', 'wraith', 'nois-family', 'spoiler', 'deceased'], 249),
  ('npc-devajo-andariel', 'Devajo Andariel — Sequence 6 Devil of the Andariel Family', 'npc', 'Devajo Andariel was a Sequence 6 Devil of the Abyss Pathway, based in Matani and Port Pylos in West Balam. A member of the Andariel Family and affiliated with the Rose School of Thought, he served as an intelligence operative for his nephew Bram Andariel, gathering information that Bram would place in the study of an empty house at 17 Aleg Street, Matani. His signature ability allowed him to completely skin humans and process them into temporary Beyonder items: wearing a victim''s skin granted him a perfect disguise as that person. During the Dream Festival of 1358 in Tizamo Town, West Balam, Devajo set off for the black ancient tomb at the center of the dream alongside a lady companion, where he summoned the Nois Family''s demon. Twice he narrowly evaded the hunger-maddened Ludwig, before fleeing back to the black ancient tomb. The Underworld Daoist there transformed him into a feathered monster that flew into the tomb and vanished. When the festival ended, only white feathers stained with light-yellow oil remained at the tomb site. He is presumed dead.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Devajo Andariel', 'Bram Andariel', 'Ludwig', 'Lumian Lee', 'Underworld Daoist'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['balam', 'west-balam', 'abyss-pathway', 'andariel-family', 'rose-school-of-thought', 'sequence-6', 'devil', 'deceased', 'dream-festival', 'disguise', 'nois-family', 'spoiler'], 226),
  ('npc-devil-dog', 'Devil Dog — Sequence 6 Abyss Creature of Backlund', 'npc', 'The Devil Dog was a large black dog owned by the Beyonder Jason Beria, elevated to Sequence 6 of the Abyss Pathway — the Devil — as part of Beria''s advancement ritual as a Desire Apostle. Residing in Backlund, it carried out a series of murders in autumn 1349, cutting open victims'' stomachs and removing their internal organs. Eleven women were killed across the initial incidents; one of those cases proved to be a copycat crime by a different hand. Klein Moretti, operating as Sherlock Moriarty, used divination and information from Derrick Berg to steer investigators toward an animal-linked Beyonder. Klein then stumbled upon the Devil Dog at its twelfth crime scene and barely escaped, aided by a mysterious woman who answered his cries for help. The murders drew a 2,000-pound reward from Sivellaus Yard. The Nighthawks located and killed the Devil Dog using Sealed Artifact 1-63, which created a battleground separated from reality. Its physical form was enormous — a large black dog with sharp white teeth bearing dark-red, rust-like stains from prolonged consumption of flesh, and its native canine scent-tracking made it an effective predator. Following its death, Jason Beria used the dog''s fate as a pretext, pretending to seek revenge in order to threaten the detectives who had investigated the case.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Devil Dog', 'Jason Beria', 'Klein Moretti', 'Derrick Berg', 'Bernadette Gustav', 'Isengard Stanton', 'Kaslana'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'abyss-pathway', 'sequence-6', 'devil', 'beyonder-creature', 'nighthawks', 'loen-kingdom', 'serial-murders', 'jason-beria', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 220),
  ('npc-bram-andariel', 'Bram Andariel — Serial Killer of Port Pylos', 'npc', 'Bram Andariel is a Sequence 7 Serial Killer of the Abyss Pathway and a descendant of the Andariel Family. Based in Port Pylos, West Balam, he operated out of an apartment on Chilicasco Street during his final months. His father bore the Andariel surname and was cut down by a curse from a Devil''s projection during a ritual gone awry; Bram inherited the resulting Beyonder status. His mother''s identity remains a mystery.

In Port Pylos, Bram pursued two goals. First, on behalf of the Andariel Family — cooperating with the Rose School of Thought — he gathered intelligence on Matani: cathedral locations, military camp details, patrol compositions, port throughput, and civilian life. Reports were deposited in the study of an empty house at 17 Aleg Street for his uncle, Devajo Andariel, to retrieve; the two never met directly. Second, he acted as an active Serial Killer, preying on individuals known for prolonged verbal cruelty and removing their lips as trophies. His murders occupied the Port Pylos patrol team for nearly two weeks, earning him a 50,000 verl pound bounty.

He was tracked down by Lumian Lee after a skirmish with a Numinous Episcopate member drew Lee''s attention. Despite anti-tracking countermeasures, Bram was cornered in his apartment and killed by fire infusion and delayed explosion. He remained a fringe figure with limited knowledge of either the Andariel Family''s wider plans or the Rose School of Thought''s true motives.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Bram Andariel', 'Devajo Andariel', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['balam', 'port-pylos', 'abyss-pathway', 'serial-killer', 'andariel-family', 'rose-school-of-thought', 'numinous-episcopate', 'bounty', 'deceased', 'spoiler', 'book-two'], 235),
  ('npc-cali', 'Cali — Penitent Padre of Tizamo Town', 'npc', 'Cali was the padre of the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun in Tizamo Town, Matani, West Balam — a native of Port Pylos with pure West Balam bloodline who rose from cathedral servant to padre through diligent service. Yearning for higher status and recognition from Northern Continent elites, he was taken to sleep at Twanaku Tupián''s house, gained lucidity, and was subsequently led to an ancient tomb during the Dream Festival, where he received a boon from the Chained Pathway, becoming a Sequence 5 Wraith without ingesting a potion. He later drew his lover Robert through the same process, enabling Robert to receive Naboredisley''s boon. During the 1358 Dream Festival, Cali helped Twanaku monitor changes in the dream, preaching and hosting naked Masses at Tizamo''s Saint-Sien Cathedral. His dream projection was killed by Lumian Lee. Afterward, wracked with genuine remorse for allowing his desires to overwhelm him, Cali sought repentance through death — dying as he believed a penitent padre should, his final words: "I''m sinful."', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Cali', 'Twanaku Tupián', 'Robert', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['balam', 'west-balam', 'tizamo-town', 'chained-pathway', 'church-of-the-eternal-blazing-sun', 'boon-recipient', 'wraith', 'dream-festival', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 211),
  ('npc-amandina', 'Amandina — Soul Assurer of Tizamo Town', 'npc', 'Amandina is a Sequence 6 Soul Assurer of the Darkness Pathway and a Boon Recipient, residing at Palms Manor in Tizamo Town, Matani, West Balam. The daughter of Sir Petit and Lady Simona, she was formerly engaged to Robert before the 1358 Dream Festival reshaped her destiny. During that festival, Robert guided her into the forest outside Tizamo Town, where she placed her hand on a massive black boulder and received a boon from the Darkness Pathway, awakening as a Beyonder. The boulder was later revealed to be an ancient tomb. Under the directive of Lumian Lee, she drew Cali into a dream to uncover the Dream Festival''s true origin. Approaching the tomb caused her to experience hallucinatory awakenings of slumbering memories, eventually revealing that an unnamed Underworld Daoist — whom she regards as her teacher — had been the individual behind her boon. The Daoist warned her to beware Penglai at the moment she secured her Soul Assurer boon. Amandina is affiliated with the Church of the Evernight Goddess and operates alongside allies Rhea, Lumian Lee, and Franca Roland.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Amandina', 'Underworld Daoist', 'Robert', 'Lumian Lee', 'Franca Roland', 'Rhea', 'Cali'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['balam', 'west-balam', 'darkness-pathway', 'soul-assurer', 'boon-recipient', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'tizamo-town', 'dream-festival', 'sequence-6', 'spoiler'], 196),
  ('npc-aiur-harson', 'Aiur Harson — Backlund Nighthawk, Sequence 7 Nightmare', 'npc', 'Aiur Harson is a Nighthawk of the Church of the Evernight Goddess stationed in the Backlund diocese. A charming middle-aged man in a gray windbreaker, he carries a thin silver sword and has attained Sequence 7 of the Darkness Pathway — the grade of Nightmare.

Aiur Harson, alongside Lorotta and Borgia, was tasked with transporting the volatile Sealed Artifact known as the Antigonus Family Puppet from Backlund to Tingen City. There, the three collaborated with the local Nighthawk chapter — including Dunn Smith — to hunt Ray Bieber, a descendant of the Antigonus Family. The operation culminated in a confrontation with the Suited Clown, a Sequence 7 Beyonder connected to the affair. Aiur survived the engagement. Though his base of operations is firmly Backlund, his involvement in the Tingen mission places him within the orbit of that city''s dramatic early events.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Aiur Harson', 'Lorotta', 'Borgia', 'Dunn Smith', 'Ray Bieber', 'Suited Clown'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'darkness-pathway', 'nightmare', 'nighthawk', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'sequence-7', 'loen-kingdom', 'sealed-artifact', 'antigonus-family', 'spoiler'], 210),
  ('npc-borgia', 'Borgia — Nighthawk of Backlund, Midnight Poet', 'npc', 'Borgia is a Nighthawk of the Church of the Evernight Goddess, stationed in the Backlund diocese. A cold man with a knife scar on the side of his face and sharp brown eyes, he is a Sequence 8 Midnight Poet of the Darkness Pathway. He operates alongside fellow Backlund Nighthawks Aiur Harson and Lorotta.

In one known operation, Borgia, Aiur Harson, and Lorotta were dispatched from Backlund to Tingen City to transport the Sealed Artifact known as the Antigonus Family Puppet. There they collaborated with the Tingen Nighthawks, including captain Dunn Smith, to hunt Ray Bieber — a descendant of the Antigonus Family. The operation escalated into a direct confrontation with the Suited Clown. His assignment to a sensitive cross-city artifact escort marks him as a trusted field operative within the Church''s law-enforcement arm.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Borgia', 'Aiur Harson', 'Lorotta', 'Dunn Smith', 'Ray Bieber'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['backlund', 'darkness-pathway', 'nighthawk', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'loen-kingdom', 'sealed-artifact', 'antigonus-family', 'spoiler'], 181),
  ('npc-seeka-tron', 'Seeka Tron — Nighthawk Midnight Poet of Tingen', 'npc', 'Seeka Tron is a Sequence 8 Midnight Poet of the Darkness Pathway and an active Nighthawk of the Blackthorn Security Company in Tingen City, Awwa County, Loen Kingdom. A devout member of the Church of the Evernight Goddess, she operates as one of the company''s field Beyonders tasked with suppressing supernatural threats.

A lady in her thirties with a few strands of graying hair, she has average looks but carries a quiet, serene demeanor and an exceptional charm. Captain Dunn Smith nicknamed her "Miss Author," a gentle jab at her persistent side vocation: she submits fiction to newspapers and magazines, though only smaller publications have accepted her work. She once petitioned Dunn directly for funds to self-publish.

Klein Moretti, in a letter to Azik Eggers, praises Seeka''s outstanding temperament, quiet personality, and remarkable courage — noting that she does not flinch even when facing death.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Seeka Tron', 'Dunn Smith', 'Klein Moretti', 'Azik Eggers'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['tingen', 'darkness-pathway', 'midnight-poet', 'nighthawk', 'blackthorn-security-company', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'loen-kingdom', 'sequence-8', 'spoiler'], 210),
  ('npc-kenley-white', 'Kenley White — Nighthawk Sleepless of Tingen', 'npc', 'Kenley White was a Sequence 9 Sleepless of the Darkness Pathway, serving as a Nighthawk under the Blackthorn Security Company in Tingen City. Originally a civilian staff member, he took the initiative to apply for full operative status — an unusual step that marked him as driven. He was not tall but toned and capable, and was known within the unit for easy sociability: he played the seven-string guitar, sang, told stories, and spoke at every card table of his unnamed fiancée. Dunn Smith later recalled him as more like a poet than Leonard.

On September 7, 1349, Kenley joined Dunn Smith and Klein Moretti in an attempt to apprehend the medium known as Madam Sharon. The operation failed. Kenley was killed by Sealed Artifact 3-0217 — the Spirit Medium''s Mirror — a death later revealed to have been arranged by Sealed Artifact 0-08, the Quill of Alzuhod. His Beyonder Characteristic was consumed by Dunn Smith. The Church of the Evernight Goddess compensated his family with 3,000 pounds; the police department added 1,000 pounds as a bereavement payment.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Kenley White', 'Dunn Smith', 'Klein Moretti', 'Sharon (Madam Sharon)', 'Leonard Mitchell'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['tingen', 'darkness-pathway', 'sleepless', 'nighthawks', 'blackthorn-security-company', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'loen-kingdom', 'deceased', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 228),
  ('npc-royale-reideen', 'Royale Reideen — Nighthawk Sleepless of Tingen', 'npc', 'Royale Reideen is a Nighthawk stationed at the Blackthorn Security Company in Tingen City, operating under the authority of the Church of the Evernight Goddess. A Sequence 9 Sleepless of the Darkness Pathway, she serves as one of the company''s field agents tasked with investigating and suppressing illegal Beyonder activity across Tingen. Cold in manner and sparing with words, Reideen carries herself with a detached professionalism that her colleagues note masks a genuine concern for the people around her. She is of Loen nationality, born within the Kingdom, and her day-to-day work involves responding to ritualistic magic incidents and other supernatural threats that fall within Nighthawk jurisdiction. Klein Moretti encountered her early in his tenure with Blackthorn, and she warned him directly of the dangers of ritualistic magic. Despite her reserve, she is regarded within the company as someone who — like Frye — quietly looks out for her colleagues, even if she rarely shows it openly, least of all at the card table.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Royale Reideen', 'Klein Moretti', 'Frye'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['tingen', 'darkness-pathway', 'sleepless', 'nighthawk', 'blackthorn-security-company', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'loen-kingdom', 'sequence-9', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 198),
  ('npc-reaza', 'Reaza — Gatekeeper of Port Pylos', 'npc', 'Reaza is a Sequence 5 Beyonder of the Death Pathway, holding the rank of Gatekeeper, and serves as Deputy Captain of Port Pylos''s Patrol Team in the Matani region of West Balam. A middle-aged man of mixed Intis and West Balam lineage, he carries a crystal skull as his primary implement and commands subordinates including Camus Castiya and Kolobo. Publicly a law-enforcement officer, Reaza secretly belongs to the Royal Family faction of the Numinous Episcopate, worshipping the deity Death under the name Salinger. When Sow — acting under Twanaku Tupián''s orders — attacks Camus using a Poker Card mystical item to forcefully possess him, Reaza intervenes decisively: he deploys an undead creature to extract the possessing Poker Card from Camus''s body, then slays Sow and other compromised patrol members. He later participates in the Dream Festival under Numinous Episcopate orders, where he summons the faction''s angel. During the festival, the entity Naboredisley emerges from the black ancient tomb at the dream''s center and kills him. As the Dream Festival ends and Reaza wakes disintegrating, Lumian Lee delivers the finishing blow, destroying his head. He dies a covert operative whose dual loyalties — civic enforcer and Numinous Episcopate asset — were never publicly exposed.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Reaza', 'Camus Castiya', 'Kolobo', 'Maslow', 'Twanaku Tupián', 'Sow', 'Lumian Lee', 'Naboredisley', 'Jenna'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['balam', 'port-pylos', 'west-balam', 'death-pathway', 'gatekeeper', 'numinous-episcopate', 'patrol-team', 'dream-festival', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 242),
  ('npc-ulika', 'Ulika — Tenebrous Deceased of the Numinous Episcopate', 'npc', 'Ulika, known by the epithet Tenebrous Deceased, is a Sequence 5 Gatekeeper of the Death pathway and a member of the Numinous Episcopate. Plump in build with dark skin and tiny dark-brown eyes, he is based out of Kolaid City in East Balam, where he serves as the Numinous Episcopate''s coordinator for its scattered field teams across Backlund on the Northern Continent. He established contact with various organizations, including Enzo of the Rose School of Thought, reflecting his role bridging the Numinous Episcopate''s Southern Continent operations with allies in the North. Following the explosion at the Black Skeleton Gang''s headquarters in Backlund, the Red Gloves launched an investigation focused on identifying formal Numinous Episcopate members in Backlund; after capturing three lesser members, they traced the network and identified Ulika as a key target. He is tracked down and killed by Daly Simone in Book 1, Chapter 908, ending the Numinous Episcopate''s coordinated presence in Backlund.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Ulika', 'Daly Simone', 'Enzo'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['balam', 'east-balam', 'death-pathway', 'numinous-episcopate', 'gatekeeper', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 206),
  ('npc-frye', 'Frye — Captain of the Tingen Nighthawks', 'npc', 'Frye is the current captain of the Nighthawks detachment stationed in Tingen City, operating under the Blackthorn Security Company and the Church of the Evernight Goddess. A pale, black-haired man in his thirties with blue eyes, a cold and gloomy temperament, and the permanent faint odour of corpses, he carries the occupational marks of years on the Death pathway. He first appeared as a Sequence 9 Corpse Collector before advancing to Gravedigger following the True Creator''s Spawn incident, then to his current rank of Sequence 7 Spirit Medium six months thereafter. Despite his unsettling demeanour, he is regarded as conscientious and warm-hearted by those who know him well, always extending aid when it is needed. He deliberately halted his advancement at Sequence 7, choosing to remain in Tingen as its protector rather than pursue higher power at the cost of his post. Before becoming a Beyonder he had aspired to be an artist; his father, a priest of the Evernight Goddess, wished him to enter the clergy, but fate drew him into the Nighthawks instead.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Frye', 'Leonard Mitchell'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['tingen', 'death-pathway', 'nighthawks', 'blackthorn-security-company', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'captain', 'sequence-7', 'spirit-medium', 'spoiler'], 218),
  ('npc-robert', 'Robert — Sequence 7 Spirit Medium of Tizamo Town', 'npc', 'Robert is a young man of Intisian origin residing in Tizamo Town, Matani, West Balam. Pale-skinned with brownish-yellow hair and a perpetually cold demeanor, he carries himself as someone long removed from ordinary sunlight. He is a Boon Recipient of the Death Pathway — Sequence 7 Spirit Medium — having received his Beyonder powers from the Underworld Daoist at a black ancient tomb in Tizamo Town rather than through conventional potion-taking. Though nominally affiliated with the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun by religion, his Beyonder allegiance runs through the Underworld Daoist, his master. His personal history is marked by loss: his relationship with former fiancée Amandina ended, and his lover Cali died. Robert remains alive as of the present day, a mid-sequence Beyonder bound to a remote Balam township, his true capabilities and the Underworld Daoist''s deeper agenda not yet fully disclosed in the public record.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Robert', 'Underworld Daoist', 'Amandina', 'Cali'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['balam', 'death-pathway', 'spirit-medium', 'boon-recipient', 'west-balam', 'tizamo-town', 'church-of-the-eternal-blazing-sun', 'intis-republic', 'sequence-7', 'spoiler'], 195),
  ('npc-lorotta', 'Lorotta — Backlund Nighthawk Gravedigger', 'npc', 'Lorotta is a Sequence 8 Gravedigger of the Death Pathway and a Nighthawk of the Backlund diocese, serving the Church of the Evernight Goddess. A black-haired woman appearing roughly thirty, she dresses in male attire — a black coat, white shirt, and tight black trousers — and is known within the Nighthawks as a master sharpshooter. Her closest operational partners are Aiur Harson and Borgia; she also maintains ties with Dunn Smith of the Tingen Nighthawks. Her most notable assignment was escorting the Sealed Artifact known as the Antigonus Family Puppet from Backlund to Tingen City, where she coordinated with the local Nighthawks to hunt Antigonus Family descendant Ray Bieber — whom the team had awoken ahead of schedule. The operation culminated in a confrontation with the Suited Clown. Off-duty, Lorotta is noted for her fondness for coffee, dessert, and maidservants. She remains alive as of current canon.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Lorotta', 'Aiur Harson', 'Borgia', 'Dunn Smith', 'Ray Bieber'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['backlund', 'death-pathway', 'nighthawk', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'loen-kingdom', 'gravedigger', 'sealed-artifact', 'antigonus-family', 'sharpshooter', 'spoiler'], 192),
  ('npc-browns-sauron', 'Browns Sauron — Affliction-Sequence Demoness of Trier', 'npc', 'Browns Sauron is a Sequence 5 Affliction Beyonder of the Demoness Pathway and a member of the Demoness Sect, bearing the bloodline of the Sauron Family. Originally from the Intis Republic, she is based in Trier and frequents the Red House Café — a venue known for women''s gatherings — as a point of contact for the Sect.

Her long orange-red hair, flowing against an otherwise clean and exquisite face, immediately drew Lumian Lee''s suspicion when he first observed her at the café. When Franca Roland, acting on orders from Madam Judgement to investigate the current state of the Primordial Demoness, visited the café and made contact, Browns handled the approach with composed professionalism. Franca expressed her intent to probe the Bliss Society and her interest in the female gatherings; Browns emphasised that the Sect places great importance on the privacy and safety of all members, and that Franca would need to undergo a formal audit before being admitted.

Her master is Clarice. She was at Sequence 6 (Pleasure) at her first appearance and had advanced to Sequence 5 (Affliction) by the later chapters of Book Two.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Browns Sauron', 'Clarice', 'Franca Roland', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'demoness-pathway', 'demoness-sect', 'sauron-family', 'sequence-5', 'affliction', 'intis-republic', 'red-house-cafe', 'book-two', 'spoiler'], 218),
  ('npc-niceea', 'Niceea — Pleasure Demoness of Trier', 'npc', 'Niceea is a Sequence 6 Pleasure of the Demoness Pathway, active in Trier within the Intis Republic. A woman with naturally wavy brown hair, deep brown eyes, red lips, and a curvy figure, she was formerly male before the Demoness pathway reshaped her. Before her Beyonder career she worked as a government spy tasked with monitoring the Emperor Party, placing her at the center of Intis''s political underground. She had recently become a Witch (Sequence 7) before advancing to Pleasure. The Demoness of Black, Clarice, assigned her as a subordinate to Franca Roland, and she now operates within that chain of command inside the Demoness Sect. Her dual background as a state intelligence operative and a Demoness Sect member gives her unusual access to both political circles and hidden Beyonder networks in Trier.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Niceea', 'Franca Roland', 'Clarice (Demoness of Black)', 'Grouès'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['trier', 'demoness-pathway', 'demoness-sect', 'emperor-party', 'intis-republic', 'sequence-6', 'pleasure', 'spy', 'beyonder', 'spoiler', 'book-2'], 197),
  ('npc-shermane', 'Shermane — Demoness Witch of East Borough', 'npc', 'Shermane is a deceased Sequence 7 Witch of the Demoness Pathway, formerly known as Sherman, a young trans woman who lived in East Borough, Backlund. For years she had suffered ostracization because she had always identified as a woman. Her path to Beyonder transformation came through Trissy, a Demoness who provided her the means to physically become the woman she had always been — at a cost. Trissy used Shermane to get close to Viscount Stratford, leveraging her relationship with him as a tool. Before her transformation, Shermane had served as one of Xio Derecha''s informants in East Borough. After becoming a Witch, she entered into a romantic relationship with Viscount Stratford. When she discovered that the Viscount had always known she was a Demoness and did not truly love her, the revelation pushed her toward Rampancy. To prevent her from becoming a Rampager, Xio Derecha killed Shermane before she could lose control. Her last words were a quiet insistence on being called by her name.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Shermane', 'Xio Derecha', 'Trissy', 'Viscount Stratford'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'east-borough', 'demoness-pathway', 'witch', 'sequence-7', 'informant', 'deceased', 'loen-kingdom', 'spoiler'], 215),
  ('npc-lewis-wien', 'Lewis Wien — Oracle of the Aurora Order, Sequence 5 Traveler', 'npc', 'Lewis Wien is a Sequence 5 Traveler of the Door Pathway and one of the twenty-two Oracles of the Aurora Order, operating under the codename Mr. X. Of medium build with raven-black curly hair and notably dark skin suggesting Feynapotter or Desi Bay heritage, he cuts a striking figure in a black classical robe, pointed mage hat, and brass mask that lends him an ancient and mysterious air. He carries the Beyonder item known as the Flower of Blood.

A former student of Dorian Gray Abraham and erstwhile member of the Abraham Family, Wien conspired with Botis — another former Abraham Family member who had risen to Saint within the Aurora Order — in a betrayal that nearly wiped out the Abraham Family''s upper echelons. He subsequently devoted himself to the Aurora Order''s agenda in the Loen Kingdom, based out of Backlund.

His activities eventually drew the attention of Fors Wall, who contracted the assassination to Gehrman Sparrow. Wien was killed in that confrontation; his soul was grazed by the Sealed Artifact Creeping Hunger, and his head was sent to Fors Wall before being delivered to Dorian Gray Abraham. His death closes a chapter of treachery that had haunted the Abraham bloodline.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Lewis Wien', 'Dorian Gray Abraham', 'Botis', 'Fors Wall', 'Klein Moretti'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['backlund', 'door-pathway', 'aurora-order', 'abraham-family', 'traitor', 'oracle', 'sequence-5', 'traveler', 'deceased', 'spoiler', 'book-one'], 233),
  ('npc-monette', 'Monette — Avatar of Amon in Trier', 'npc', 'Monette is a slender young man of Fog Sea Islander descent who poses as a swindler and former tenant of the Auberge du Coq Doré Hotel in Trier. He is, in truth, one of Amon''s avatars — a fact confirmed to Lumian Lee by Fors Wall after Lumian first encountered him in Underground Trier. Operating under cover of petty fraud, Monette claims to have been twice-conned by Salle de Bal Unique share promoters before joining the dance hall''s orbit himself, becoming an affiliate of Salle de Bal Unique in Trier''s Quartier de l''Observatoire. He carries a transparent monocle worn on his right eye; when he dons it, observers sense an uncanny shift in his character — a subtle wrongness that unsettles even those with Beyonder awareness. In Trier''s catacombs he played the role of tomb adventurer, covertly stealing and returning an Earth Blood ore specimen to engineer Lumian''s unwitting transport of it to the Samaritan Women''s Spring. He later commissioned the theft of a tearcatcher from the Thorns and Shieldwall Tomb, seemingly targeting the Mirror World Fragment concealed within. Hela identified him as tied to the Amon Family of the Fourth Epoch. As an avatar of Amon — apex of the Error Pathway — his displayed sequence within this guise remains deliberately obscured.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Monette', 'Amon', 'Lumian Lee', 'Fors Wall', 'Charlie Collent', 'Hela', 'Xio Derecha', 'Jenna', 'Termiboros'], ARRAY[0], ARRAY['trier', 'error-pathway', 'amon-family', 'salle-de-bal-unique', 'avatar', 'underground-trier', 'catacombs', 'swindler', 'fourth-epoch', 'spoiler'], 213),
  ('npc-rosago', 'Rosago — Marionettist of the Secret Order', 'npc', 'Rosago is a Sequence 5 Marionettist of the Fool Pathway, operating in Backlund as both a member of the Secret Order and an operative of Intis Republic intelligence. A gentleman of Intisian origin with black hair and blue eyes, he presents a polished exterior that belies the dangerous capabilities of a mid-sequence Beyonder. Acting on orders from Bakerland — the Intis Ambassador and intelligence chief in Loen — he was dispatched to assassinate Sherlock Moriarty, in truth the Sequence 8 Klein Moretti. He employed advance divination to anticipate threats, yet was nonetheless killed in September 1349 through the combined efforts of Klein and the Beyonder Sharron, aided by the Language of Foulness. His death proved highly consequential: Klein recovered Fool Pathway formulas up to Sequence 5 and the All-Black Eye, while Sharron claimed his Notary Certificate. Rosago''s brief appearance illustrates both the Secret Order''s reach into Backlund and the Intis intelligence apparatus''s willingness to expend mid-sequence assets against perceived threats.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Rosago', 'Klein Moretti', 'Sharron', 'Bakerland Jean Madan'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['backlund', 'fool-pathway', 'secret-order', 'intis-republic', 'marionettist', 'assassin', 'intelligence-operative', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 214),
  ('npc-leah-bellot', 'Leah Bellot — Bureau 8 Major and Fool Pathway Magician', 'npc', 'Leah Bellot is a Sequence 7 Magician of the Fool Pathway, serving as a Major within Bureau 8, the military special department of the Intis Republic under the Intis Intelligence and Homeland Security Committee. Originally from Bigorre in Riston Province, she is stationed in Trier and operates as part of a joint investigative team alongside Valentine de Lacourt and Ryan Vitia. The trio traveled to Cordu Village to investigate a mysterious case, only to find themselves trapped in the village''s time loop until Lumian Lee informed them of their situation; they subsequently cooperated with him to break free. Leah is striking in appearance — long light-gray hair tied in an elaborate bun, a white veil atop her head, and two tiny silver bells fastened to her veil and boots that jingle as she walks. She is considered socially adept, naturally building operational trust through conversation. Her divination abilities have guided her assessments of key persons of interest, as when she used divination results to evaluate Lumian Lee. After the Cordu incident, she was later spotted entering the Alone Bar in Trier, confirming an ongoing Bureau 8 presence in the city.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Leah Bellot', 'Valentine de Lacourt', 'Ryan Vitia', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['trier', 'fool-pathway', 'bureau-8', 'intis-republic', 'major', 'intelligence', 'divination', 'cordu-village', 'spoiler'], 205),
  ('npc-hanass-vincent', 'Hanass Vincent — Secrets Suppliant of Tingen', 'npc', 'Hanass Vincent was a rather famous fortune-teller and resident mentor of the Divination Club in Tingen City, charging four soli per reading. Adept at multiple divination methods, he held the rank of Secrets Suppliant — Sequence 9 of the Hanged Man pathway — and served as a covert member of the Aurora Order under the authority of Mr. Z.

Together with his associate Sirius Arapis, Vincent obtained the Antigonus Family''s Notebook through an unknown source. Fearing pursuit by the Secret Order, he chose to pass the notebook to Welch McGovern, presenting it as an ordinary ancient book — a transaction that inadvertently set the events of Klein Moretti''s awakening in motion.

Following the incident at Selena Wood''s banquet, the Nighthawks launched an investigation into Vincent. Before he could be formally questioned, Nighthawk Dunn Smith snuck into his dream and glimpsed a clear image of the True Creator. The shock triggered a fatal heart attack in Vincent during his sleep. His disciple Selena Wood survived him; his role as an Aurora Order operative and original handler of the Notebook remained a key thread in the Tingen arc.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Hanass Vincent', 'Sirius Arapis', 'Selena Wood', 'Welch McGovern', 'Mr. Z', 'Dunn Smith'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['tingen', 'hanged-man-pathway', 'aurora-order', 'divination-club', 'true-creator', 'secrets-suppliant', 'sequence-9', 'antigonus-notebook', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 233),
  ('npc-osta-trul', 'Osta Trul — Secrets Suppliant of Underground Trier', 'npc', 'Osta Trul is a con artist and Sequence 9 Secrets Suppliant of the Hanged Man Pathway, operating in the shadowed alleys of Underground Trier. Originally from Cécilis Province in the Intis Republic, he arrived in Trier over a decade ago chasing wealth that never materialised. Drawn into real mysticism through enthusiast magazines and gatherings, he eventually accepted an invitation to a gathering with genuine Beyonder powers — an encounter that permanently altered his course. A few months before the events of Book Two, he borrowed 3,000 verl d''or from a contact named Brignais to fund the main ingredient of his Secrets Suppliant potion, attaining his sequence at considerable personal debt. He worships at the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun and maintains a residence at 20th Rue des Blouses Blanches, fifth floor. On the surface he performs as a warlock for tourists and locals — a useful cover that obscures his genuine, if low-ranking, Beyonder status. He was targeted as an intelligence objective by the Tarot Club''s Magician, who tasked Lumian Lee with earning his trust, likely in connection with Mr. K''s gatherings.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Osta Trul', 'Lumian Lee', 'Fors Wall', 'Brignais', 'Mr. K'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['trier', 'hanged-man-pathway', 'underground-trier', 'sequence-9', 'secrets-suppliant', 'church-of-the-eternal-blazing-sun', 'intis-republic', 'con-artist', 'book-two', 'spoiler'], 235),
  ('npc-professor', 'Professor — Constellations Master of the Hermit Pathway', 'npc', 'Known only by her codename, Professor is a Transmigrator from the Modern Era residing in Trier, Intis Republic, and a Sequence 5 Constellations Master of the Hermit Pathway. She operates within the Academy Faction of the Curly-Haired Baboons Research Society, where she presents herself in a black butterfly mask, white shirt with bow tie, long dark coat, and a typeset paper name tag bearing her codename. She was also a former member of the Moses Ascetic Order. A few years before 1358, their shared codename led to an unexpected encounter with a fellow Research Society member known as Associate Professor; the two eventually married. Together with other Society members who had belonged to the Moses Ascetic Order, Professor organized an offline gathering at 6 Rue Belfort on Avenue du Boulevard in Trier, extending a particular invitation to the transmigrator Muggle — partly out of friendship, partly to solicit her support for an Order beset by mounting difficulties. During Project Vortex, the transmission of the Outer Deity known as the Inextinguishable Ravings through the planet''s barrier reached Professor and Associate Professor alongside other Hermit Pathway Beyonders.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Professor', 'Associate Professor', 'Aurore Lee (Muggle)'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'hermit-pathway', 'sequence-5', 'constellations-master', 'transmigrator', 'curly-haired-baboons-research-society', 'moses-ascetic-order', 'intis-republic', 'spoiler'], 185),
  ('npc-leon', 'Leon — Warlock Bishop of the Sick Church', 'npc', 'Leon is a Sequence 7 Warlock of the Hermit Pathway and a bishop of the Sick Church, based in Trier within the Intis Republic. As a mid-sequence Beyonder of the Hermit line, he operates within the ecclesiastical hierarchy of the Sick Church, an organization known for its unconventional doctrines and Beyonder affiliations. His recorded superiors are Lugano Toscano and Jenna, placing him in a subordinate but established clerical role within that body. Leon functions as an institutional representative of the Sick Church in Trier, wielding the esoteric capabilities of a Warlock in service to that organization. His vital status is recorded as alive. Beyond his rank and affiliation, the public record of his individual deeds remains sparse, making him a figure defined more by his institutional position than by singular canon acts.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Leon', 'Lugano Toscano', 'Jenna'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['trier', 'hermit-pathway', 'sick-church', 'bishop', 'warlock', 'intis-republic', 'mid-sequence', 'spoiler'], 176),
  ('npc-associate-professor', 'Associate Professor — Hermit Pathway Transmigrator, Curly-Haired Baboons Research Society', 'npc', 'Known only by his codename within the Curly-Haired Baboons Research Society, the Associate Professor is a male Transmigrator from the Modern Era residing in Trier, Intis Republic. He is a Beyonder of the Hermit Pathway and a member of the Society''s Academy Faction. He and fellow member Professor — later his wife — met in real life after their shared codename drew them together. Both are former members of the Moses Ascetic Order. In the Research Society''s anonymous gatherings he appears as a slender man with a brownish-yellow manila document bag obscuring his face. He helped organize a clandestine offline meeting at 6 Rue Belfort on Avenue du Boulevard in Trier, where fellow member Muggle (Aurore Lee) was specially invited so the group could solicit her backing — and that of her powerful unknown patron — for the Moses Ascetic Order amid mounting difficulties. During Project Vortex, when the Outer Deity Inextinguishable Ravings broadcast through the planet''s barrier, he and Professor were among the Hermit Pathway Beyonders affected by the transmission.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Associate Professor', 'Professor', 'Aurore Lee'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'hermit-pathway', 'curly-haired-baboons-research-society', 'moses-ascetic-order', 'transmigrator', 'academy-faction', 'intis-republic', 'spoiler'], 223),
  ('npc-frunziar-edward', 'Frunziar Edward — Lost Soldier of Groselle''s Travels', 'npc', 'Frunziar Edward was a Loen Kingdom soldier who vanished 165 years before the story''s present day. His last known address was 18 Delahire Street, Northwest Borough, Backlund. He was in truth trapped inside the mystical tome Groselle''s Travels, living as a character within its self-contained world alongside companions Groselle, Siatas, Snowman, and Mobet Zoroast. With their help he climbed the Justiciar Pathway to Sequence 5 — Disciplinary Paladin. The potion he consumed was illusory, conjured by the book''s power, so his corpse left no Beyonder Characteristic. He died after his release, and Klein Moretti placed his ashes in the Church of the Lord of Storms cemetery outside West Borough, Backlund. His epitaph reads: "Every journey has its destination." A man of quiet faith in the Lord of Storms, he is remembered as someone who found purpose even in captivity, though he always sensed he did not truly belong in the world the book had made for him.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Frunziar Edward', 'Groselle', 'Siatas', 'Snowman', 'Mobet Zoroast', 'Edwina Edwards', 'Klein Moretti', 'Anderson Hood', 'Danitz'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['backlund', 'justiciar-pathway', 'sequence-5', 'disciplinary-paladin', 'loen-kingdom', 'church-of-the-lord-of-storms', 'groselles-travels', 'deceased', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 220),
  ('npc-moran-avigny', 'Moran Avigny — Minister of Industry, Mirror Person', 'npc', 'Moran Avigny served as Minister of Industry of the Intis Republic, operating out of Trier. A man of distinguished bearing in his late sixties — gray-haired, dark-gray-eyed, exuding a refined elegance befitting the Intisian establishment — he concealed a far darker nature beneath that polished exterior: he was a Mirror Person, a human fused with the mirror world. Avigny had advanced to Sequence 5 within the Justiciar pathway, holding the rank of Disciplinary Paladin. He was affiliated with both the Mirror People and the School of Truth, and worshipped the Chaos Demoness. His family connection ran through the Tamara bloodline; his daughter, Delilah Le Roy, bore that name but was traced back to him through Magic Mirror Divination conducted by Franca Roland and analysis by Anthony Reid after Jenna detected tremors from her Mirror World Fragment during performances at the Tamara family tomb. That investigation led directly to his exposure. Avigny was ultimately slain by Franca Roland and Jenna, bringing his tenure as a concealed Mirror Person in high Intisian office to an end.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Moran Avigny', 'Franca Roland', 'Jenna', 'Jebus Lata', 'Delilah Le Roy', 'Anthony Reid'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'justiciar-pathway', 'mirror-people', 'school-of-truth', 'chaos-demoness', 'intis-republic', 'tamara-family', 'minister-of-industry', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 213),
  ('npc-harras', 'Harras — Sequence 6 Judge, Capim''s Strongest Surveillant', 'npc', 'Harras is a middle-aged Beyonder of the Justiciar Pathway, holding Sequence 6 as a Judge. He operates in Backlund, Loen Kingdom, serving as the strongest among the surveillants answering to Capim. Distinguished by his black tailcoat, white wig, and a long, thin, stern face with a naturally pursed mouth, Harras projects an air of rigid authority befitting his pathway''s nature.

Though personally a Sequence 6, Harras wields an iron-black metal glove equivalent in power to a Sequence 5 Disciplinary Paladin — an artifact that substantially amplifies his combat capability. During an encounter at Capim''s villa, he was heavily injured by Klein Moretti and, on the brink of losing control of his Beyonder characteristics, used the ability "Exile" on Klein and quickly escaped. His associates at the villa include Capim, Parker, Katy, and Belize. He enforces strict secrecy among all present at the villa, warning them against leaking anything they witness.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Harras', 'Capim', 'Parker', 'Katy', 'Belize'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'justiciar-pathway', 'sequence-6', 'judge', 'surveillant', 'loen-kingdom', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 220),
  ('npc-belize', 'Belize — Surveillant of Capim', 'npc', 'Belize is a Sequence 7 Interrogator of the Justiciar pathway, stationed in Backlund as one of Capim''s personal surveillants. A bearded man of unknown age, he is recognisable by his frighteningly cold blue eyes. He is equipped with a high-pressure steam rifle and golden bullets. Assigned to guard the basement of Capim''s villa, Belize chose to flee when the estate was attacked by Klein Moretti rather than mount a defence. He operates alongside fellow surveillants Parker, Harras, and Katy within the network of enforcers surrounding Capim. His Beyonder abilities reflect the Justiciar pathway''s emphasis on law, interrogation, and coercion.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Belize', 'Capim', 'Parker', 'Harras', 'Katy'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'justiciar-pathway', 'sequence-7', 'interrogator', 'surveillant', 'loen-kingdom', 'spoiler', 'book-one'], 148),
  ('npc-katy', 'Katy — Interrogator of Capim''s Surveillance Ring', 'npc', 'Ma''am Katy was a Sequence 7 Interrogator of the Justiciar Pathway, operating in Backlund as one of Capim''s surveillants. A scarred, cruel-edged operative, she worked alongside fellow agents Parker, Harras, and Belize under Capim''s direction. Armed with a revolver, Beyonder bullets, and a whip, she carried the tools of both mundane enforcement and Beyonder coercion. Her Interrogator abilities placed her squarely in the mid-sequence tier, capable of extracting information through means beyond ordinary interrogation. She met her end at Capim''s villa when Klein Moretti killed her during a confrontation; her Beyonder characteristic was subsequently sold to Xio Derecha. Katy leaves no lasting organizational footprint — she was an instrument of Capim''s network rather than a power in her own right — but her death marked an early milestone in Klein''s escalating entanglements with Backlund''s Beyonder underworld.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Katy', 'Capim', 'Klein Moretti', 'Parker', 'Harras', 'Belize', 'Xio Derecha'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'justiciar-pathway', 'interrogator', 'sequence-7', 'capim-network', 'deceased', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 195),
  ('npc-parker', 'Parker — Sequence 8 Sheriff, Capim''s Surveillant', 'npc', 'Parker, known to associates as Mr. Parker, was a Sequence 8 Sheriff of the Justiciar Pathway operating in Backlund during the early chapters of the game''s present era. Slightly taller than 1.70 metres, he appeared somewhat old, with wrinkles and a high nose bridge. His brown eyes were filled with spirit, though he carried no particular look of deterrence. He served as one of the surveillants under Capim, working alongside fellow operatives Katy, Harras, and Belize to monitor targets of interest at Capim''s Villa. Parker''s death came swiftly: he was killed by Klein Moretti during a confrontation at the villa. In the aftermath, his Beyonder characteristic was sold through Fors Wall to Xio Derecha, making even his end a transactional footnote in Backlund''s underground Beyonder economy. Parker represents the rank-and-file of Backlund''s mid-tier Beyonder underworld — competent enough to hold a sequence but not powerful enough to survive contact with a rising star on the Fool''s path.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Parker', 'Capim', 'Klein Moretti', 'Katy', 'Harras', 'Belize', 'Fors Wall', 'Xio Derecha'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['backlund', 'justiciar-pathway', 'sequence-8', 'sheriff', 'beyonder', 'deceased', 'book-one', 'loen-kingdom', 'surveillant', 'spoiler'], 220),
  ('npc-kaslana', 'Kaslana — Beyonder Detective of Backlund', 'npc', 'Kaslana is a private detective and Beyonder of the Justiciar Pathway operating out of Backlund. A woman of around thirty, she has black hair and blue eyes, and her features carry the practical wear of someone long accustomed to difficult cases rather than social graces. She was one of four detectives enlisted by Rogo Colloman to protect his son Adol, alongside Isengard Stanton, Sherlock Moriarty, and others. The group held detective meetings organized by Isengard Stanton to work through a serial killer case. After that case concluded, several detectives who had been involved received threatening letters. Led by Kaslana, they paid a visit to Sherlock Moriarty''s residence to discuss the threat and coordinate a response. Lydia serves as her personal assistant. Her precise sequence on the Justiciar Pathway is unconfirmed — the wiki infobox leaves both sequence name and rank blank — though her hands-on street-level investigative work, with no recorded exceptional feats, is consistent with an entry-level position; Sequence 9 on the Justiciar Pathway is Arbiter.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Kaslana', 'Isengard Stanton', 'Klein Moretti', 'Lydia'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['backlund', 'justiciar-pathway', 'detective', 'loen-kingdom', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 191),
  ('npc-rus-bathory', 'Rus Báthory — Sanguine Baron and Potions Professor', 'npc', 'Rus Báthory is a Sanguine Baron residing in Backlund, Loen Kingdom, and a Sequence 6 Potions Professor of the Moon pathway. Thin-faced but charming, he is an antique enthusiast with a particular fondness for strange trinkets from the Southern Continent. On the orders of Nibbs Odora, his grandson Cosmi gathered a small group of Sanguines — Báthory among them — and tasked them with hunting down believers of the Primordial Moon. To bait his targets, Báthory surreptitiously offered the Moon Puppet for sale at a Beyonder Gathering; Windsor Behring, a known Primordial Moon believer on the Sanguine hit list, purchased it, confirming her identity. Fors Wall, who had attended the same gathering, recognised Windsor and sold the information to Emlyn White through the Tarot Club network. Tracking the Moon Puppet''s resonance, Báthory located Windsor and fought her directly, sustaining severe injuries in the process. Emlyn White, who had been covertly shadowing him, then intervened and finished Windsor off, claiming the kill for himself.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Rus Báthory', 'Emlyn White', 'Cosmi Odora', 'Nibbs Odora', 'Windsor Behring', 'Fors Wall'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'moon-pathway', 'sanguine', 'potions-professor', 'sequence-6', 'primordial-moon', 'beyonder-gathering', 'loen-kingdom', 'spoiler'], 210),
  ('npc-waymandy', 'Waymandy — Sanguine Baron and Self-Proclaimed Historian of Backlund', 'npc', 'Baron Waymandy is a Sanguine of the Moon pathway, holding the rank of Sequence 6 Potions Professor. Over two centuries old, he resides in Hillston Borough, Backlund, where he fashions himself a historian — a reputation his peers note with mild amusement. His black hair is combed back neatly; he carries the look of a composed gentleman in his early thirties, betraying none of his true age. A known figure among Backlund''s Sanguine community, Waymandy was recommended to Emlyn White by Emlyn''s father as a source of arcane historical knowledge. Emlyn sought him out while investigating the City of Silver, and Waymandy proved the reputation well-earned: he revealed that the ancient Kingdom of Silver had worshipped a queen of the Giant King''s Court, Omebella. His willingness to share such esoteric lore makes him a quiet but consequential node in Backlund''s supernatural information network — a living archive of pre-modern Beyonder history.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Waymandy', 'Emlyn White', 'Nibbs Odora', 'Omebella'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'moon-pathway', 'sanguine', 'sequence-6', 'potions-professor', 'historian', 'giant-kings-court', 'city-of-silver', 'loen-kingdom', 'hillston-borough', 'spoiler'], 204),
  ('npc-windsor-behring', 'Windsor Behring — Potions Professor of the Primordial Moon', 'npc', 'Windsor Behring is a female human Beyonder active in Backlund, assessed as a likely Sequence 6 Potions Professor of the Moon Pathway and a believer of the Primordial Moon. Dark-skinned, with thin brows and the corners of her mouth drooping significantly, she is marked on a Sanguine hit list targeting Primordial Moon adherents.

She attends a Beyonder Gathering and purchases the Moon Puppet, an artefact connected to the Primordial Moon — unaware that it is bait planted by the Sanguine Rus Báthory to locate believers like her. Fors Wall, also present at the gathering, recognises Windsor from intelligence Emlyn White had previously shared through the Tarot Club, and passes this identification to Emlyn. Grasping Rus Báthory''s ploy, Emlyn resolves to follow the Sanguine hunter and claim the target himself. Rus tracks Windsor through the Moon Puppet, and the two fight — she inflicts severe injuries on him before Emlyn White, shadowing Rus in secret, steps in and snaps her neck, killing her.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Windsor Behring', 'Emlyn White', 'Rus Báthory', 'Fors Wall'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'moon-pathway', 'primordial-moon', 'beyonder', 'sequence-6', 'potions-professor', 'sanguine-target', 'tarot-club-adjacent', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 210),
  ('npc-argos', 'Argos — Sequence 7 Vampire, Primordial Moon Believer', 'npc', 'Argos is a male human Beyonder of the Moon Pathway, having attained Sequence 7 Vampire. A devout follower of the Primordial Moon — the Mother Goddess of Depravity — he operated within Backlund and was among those placed on a formal hunt list issued by the Sanguine, the vampire clan that worships their ancestor Lilith. The Sanguine viewed Primordial Moon believers such as Argos and his close associate Galis Kevin as heretics to be purified, reflecting the deep theological schism between the two strands of the Moon Pathway. Emlyn White, acting on intelligence supplied by Ian Wright, tracked Argos to his location in Backlund. Both Argos and Galis Kevin were killed in the same encounter; Argos met his end by Sun Water — the classical purification agent used against vampires — administered by Emlyn White. His death is one of the early acts confirming Emlyn White as a capable enforcer of Sanguine doctrine against wayward Moon Pathway practitioners.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Argos', 'Galis Kevin', 'Emlyn White', 'Ian Wright'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'moon-pathway', 'vampire', 'primordial-moon', 'sanguine', 'deceased', 'book-one', 'spoiler', 'loen-kingdom'], 185),
  ('npc-galis-kevin', 'Galis Kevin — Sequence 7 Vampire of the Moon Pathway', 'npc', 'Galis Kevin is a male mixed-blood Beyonder active in Backlund during the Book One era. A follower of the Mother Goddess of Depravity, he holds Sequence 7 on the Moon Pathway — the rank of Vampire. His partial transformation is apparent in his eyes, which are slightly red but fall short of a full Sanguine''s gaze, suggesting incomplete acquisition of sanguine characteristics.

His allegiance to the Primordial Moon placed him on a kill list issued by the Sanguines targeting Primordial Moon believers. He operated in Backlund alongside a fellow believer, Argos. His whereabouts were uncovered when Emlyn White, a Sanguine, acquired intelligence through Ian Wright. White located Galis Kevin and Argos together and killed them both — snapping Kevin''s neck — in Book One, Chapter 795.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Galis Kevin', 'Argos', 'Emlyn White', 'Ian Wright'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'moon-pathway', 'vampire', 'primordial-moon', 'sanguine', 'deceased', 'antagonist', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 195),
  ('npc-la-nou-bruch', 'La Nou Bruch — Sanguine of the Bruch Family', 'npc', 'La Nou Bruch is a Sanguine belonging to the Bruch family, active in the city of Trier. He is a Sequence 7 Vampire on the Moon Pathway — a rank he insists be named correctly, taking quick offence at anyone who mistakes his kind for ordinary vampires.

Tall and slender with a prominent nose bridge, impeccably groomed medium-length black hair, fair skin, and striking red eyes, he carries an androgynous allure alongside aristocratic pride in his Sanguine heritage. He was apprehended by Lumian Lee while harvesting Mandrakes at the Rois Comprehensive Execution Ground in Trier. His stated purpose was practical: the Mandrakes were intended to suppress the spirituality surges that all Sanguines had been suffering during full moons — a phenomenon tied to the awakening of the Sanguine Ancestor Lilith and Her reclamation of Moon Pathway authority from the Evernight Goddess.

His affiliation rests with the Sanguines broadly and the Bruch family specifically. He remains alive as of his encounter with Lumian Lee, a mid-sequence figure whose activities in Trier place him within the Intis Republic''s supernatural underground.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['La Nou Bruch', 'Lumian Lee', 'Lilith'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['trier', 'moon-pathway', 'sanguines', 'bruch-family', 'vampire', 'intis-republic', 'book-two', 'spoiler'], 225),
  ('npc-christo', 'Christo — "Rat," Beast Tamer of the Savoie Mob', 'npc', 'Known on Trier''s underworld circuit as "Rat," Christo is a slender man of below-average height, distinguished by pronounced rat-like whiskers and dark blue eyes beneath a crown of thick grayish-black hair. He holds leadership rank within the Savoie Mob and personally oversees the organization''s smuggling operations. A Sequence 8 Beyonder of the Moon Pathway, his abilities as a Beast Tamer manifest in an affinity for animals — most visibly in two companions he keeps close: Taffy, a palm-sized white rat with ruby-bright eyes capable of sensing hidden dangers and gauging the approximate strength of others, and a colorful triangular-headed snake. Christo worships at the Church of the God of Steam and Machinery and is married. He is tied emotionally to the city through personal loss: his younger brother Erkin, a member of a goods-delivery crew, disappeared somewhere in Underground Trier and was ultimately confirmed dead. That disappearance drew Christo to the Salle de Bal Brise to petition the Mob''s senior figures for help — the moment he first surfaced in recorded accounts. He operates squarely within Trier''s criminal infrastructure, using Mob channels and beast-augmented instincts to keep illicit shipments moving through the city.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Christo', 'Erkin', 'Taffy'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['trier', 'moon-pathway', 'savoie-mob', 'beast-tamer', 'sequence-8', 'underworld', 'smuggling', 'church-of-the-god-of-steam-and-machinery', 'spoiler'], 235),
  ('npc-glaint', 'Glaint — Viscount Apothecary of Backlund', 'npc', 'Viscount Glaint is a young Loen nobleman based in Backlund who inherited his title at the age of twenty following his father''s early death. A dedicated mysticism enthusiast, he occupies the Sequence 9 position on the Moon Pathway as an Apothecary — a choice he made deliberately, believing that personal health and immunity to serious illness and harm are life''s paramount concerns. His social circle overlaps with other genteel Beyonders: he shares mysticism discussions with Audrey Hall and personally introduced her to Fors Wall, a connection that quietly shaped Backlund''s informal Beyonder network during the early Sequence years. He provided the Apothecary potion formula to assist in freeing Xio Derecha from custody, demonstrating a willingness to use his resources on behalf of allies. When the 1350 World War began, Glaint answered the call alongside other young Loen nobles, taking on a commissioned officer''s role in the army. He remains alive, a low-sequence Moon Pathway practitioner embedded in Backlund''s aristocratic and mysticism-curious social strata.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Glaint', 'Audrey Hall', 'Fors Wall', 'Xio Derecha'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['backlund', 'moon-pathway', 'apothecary', 'loen-kingdom', 'nobility', 'viscount', 'low-sequence', 'mysticism-enthusiast', '1350-world-war', 'spoiler'], 211),
  ('npc-lugano-toscano', 'Lugano Toscano — Druid of the Sick Church', 'npc', 'Lugano Toscano is a burly, refined-featured man in his mid-thirties from Riston Province in the Intis Republic, currently serving as Archbishop of the Sick Church. A former bounty hunter who used the Dariège mountain ranges to smuggle wanted criminals between Feynapotter and Intis, Lugano stumbled into the Beyonder world by consuming the Characteristic of his old contact Tanko — a Planter on the Mother Pathway — ignoring the dying man''s wish to pass it to a Blessed of the Church of the Earth Mother. This act of greed placed him on the Mother Pathway. In Trier, seeking funds to advance to Sequence 8 Doctor, he attached himself to Lumian Lee (operating as Ciel Dubois), managing and guarding the Salle de Gristmill for the Savoie Mob. When the Savoie Mob''s links to the Iron and Blood Cross Order made him a wanted man, Lumian recruited him as a translator for a mission to Feynapotter, where he also served as Ludwig''s caretaker. He converted toward the Church of the Earth Mother under Montserrat''s influence and demonstrated unusual lucidity during the 1358 Dream Festival. His loyalty to Lumian is unswerving.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Lugano Toscano', 'Lumian Lee', 'Tanko', 'Ludwig', 'Jenna', 'Montserrat'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'mother-pathway', 'sick-church', 'savoie-mob', 'church-of-the-earth-mother', 'bounty-hunter', 'book-two', 'spoiler', 'intis-republic'], 237),
  ('npc-cielf-june', 'Cielf June — Artisan of the Paragon Pathway', 'npc', 'Cielf June is a Sequence 6 Artisan of the Paragon pathway, a thin, tanned middle-aged man who hid in Bayam after betraying the Church of the God of Steam and Machinery. A secret descendant of Ciel Gustav — eldest son of Emperor Roselle — he traded enchanted creations only with trusted acquaintances, sustaining a life of fine wines and beauties. Members of the Rose School of Thought discovered and controlled him; tempted by the Primordial Moon, he became a follower of the Mother Goddess of Depravity, his Spirit Body corrupted toward conjoined-person status. Alger Wilson and Cattleya used Frank Lee''s mushroom to eliminate the Rose School operatives; Bernadette Gustav confirmed his bloodline from a blood sample. Cattleya brought him aboard The Future as part of the Stars Pirates, assigning him as experimental assistant to Frank Lee — leaving Cielf traumatized by mushroom-reproduction experiments. His creations include the Gargoyle Glasses, Gold Mask, Hand of Horror, Lie, Whip of Mind, Wintry Blade, and Word of the Sea. He was later separated from Frank and sent to Bernadette''s care after the significance of the Mother Pathway became apparent.', null, 5, 'bayam', ARRAY['Cielf June', 'Alger Wilson', 'Cattleya', 'Bernadette Gustav', 'Frank Lee', 'Roselle Gustav', 'Ciel Gustav'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['bayam', 'paragon-pathway', 'stars-pirates', 'church-of-steam-and-machinery', 'rose-school-of-thought', 'primordial-moon', 'mother-goddess-of-depravity', 'gustav-family', 'artisan', 'sequence-6', 'spoiler'], 240),
  ('npc-ciel-gustav', 'Ciel Gustav — Eldest Son of Emperor Roselle', 'npc', 'Ciel Gustav was the eldest son of Emperor Roselle Gustav and his wife Matilda Abel, born into the ruling family of the Intis Republic and raised in Trier. A prince of the republic by blood, Ciel followed the Paragon Pathway — the pathway of knowledge and invention championed by the Church of the God of Steam and Machinery. He attained a low-sequence rank within that tradition, though the precise title he held is unrecorded.

Ciel did not long outlive his father. When Emperor Roselle was assassinated, the shock and dread overwhelmed him; he died shortly afterward, consumed by horror and grief. In the political turbulence that followed, the Sauron family sought to hang or exile his descendants, but the Church of Steam intervened and sheltered the Gustav line by enrolling them as clergymen. Ciel''s own descendant Cielf June would carry the family name into later generations under that ecclesiastical protection. His siblings — older sister Bernadette Gustav and younger brother Bornova Gustav — survived him.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Ciel Gustav', 'Roselle Gustav', 'Matilda Abel', 'Bernadette Gustav', 'Bornova Gustav', 'Cielf June'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['trier', 'church-of-steam', 'gustav-family', 'intis-republic', 'deceased', 'prince', 'low-sequence', 'spoiler'], 215),
  ('npc-ikanser-bernard', 'Ikanser Bernard — Deacon of the Machinery Hivemind', 'npc', 'Ikanser Bernard is a male Beyonder of the Paragon Pathway and a Deacon of the Machinery Hivemind, an arm of the Church of the God of Steam and Machinery. He is stationed in Backlund, the capital of the Loen Kingdom. Bernard is most closely associated with the custody and deployment of Sealed Artifact 2-111, known as Arrodes — a powerful and unpredictable sealed item — which he employed to lead a Hivemind investigation into events at an abandoned warehouse district. Later, he took charge of inspecting a residence connected to Sherlock Moriarty after it was infiltrated by the Desire Apostle Jason Beria, demonstrating his counter-supernatural field role. He nominally presents as a believer of the Church of the God of Steam and Machinery, though this affiliation doubles as operational cover. During the 1350 World War, Bernard and his Hivemind colleagues engaged in direct combat against Nighthawk forces. He is noted for pragmatic tactical awareness, acknowledging that even expert preparation cannot guarantee the suppression of divination.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Ikanser Bernard', 'Klein Moretti', 'Sharron', 'Maric', 'Steve', 'Jason Beria'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'paragon-pathway', 'machinery-hivemind', 'church-of-steam-and-machinery', 'deacon', 'loen-kingdom', 'sealed-artifact', 'arrodes', 'nighthawks', 'world-war-1350', 'spoiler'], 222),
  ('npc-albus-medici', 'Albus Medici — Reaper of the Iron and Blood Cross Order', 'npc', 'Albus Medici is a living male Beyonder in Trier, Intis Republic. A member of the Medici Family — descendants of the Red Angel Medici, a King of Angels who bore the Uniqueness of the Red Priest Pathway — Albus holds Sequence 5, bearing the title Reaper. He is affiliated with the Iron and Blood Cross Order and with the Red of War and Black Cat groups.

As a member of the Red of War rebuilt by his ancestor, Albus can concentrate his power toward that progenitor, receive a share in return, and distribute part of the damage he sustains.

Abrasive and provocative, he rarely filters his speech. He was present at Ciel Dubois''s first Iron and Blood Cross Order meeting at Gardner Martin''s residence on 11 Rue des Fontaines, Trier, and aided in capturing the padre of Cordu Village, Guillaume Bénet. He joined an expedition into the underground maze of Red Swan Castle with Ciel Dubois and Elros Einhorn at the behest of Poufer Sauron, participated in the civil unrest the Order orchestrated before the door to Fourth Epoch Trier opened, and was later encountered in Morora.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Albus Medici', 'Medici', 'Ciel Dubois', 'Gardner Martin', 'Guillaume Bénet', 'Elros Einhorn', 'Poufer Sauron'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'red-priest-pathway', 'iron-and-blood-cross-order', 'medici-family', 'red-of-war', 'black-cat', 'sequence-5', 'reaper', 'intis-republic', 'spoiler'], 249),
  ('npc-gardner-martin', 'Gardner Martin — Reaper and Boss of the Savoie Mob', 'npc', 'Gardner Martin is a Sequence 5 Reaper of the Red Priest pathway and the undisputed boss of the Savoie Mob in Trier. A native of Savoie province in the Intis Republic, he built a facade of respectability as a merchant: shareholder of the Rist Docks, head of Rist Shipping Company, and shareholder of Savoie Construction Company, enterprises that employ Savoyards throughout the city. Behind that veneer he answers to the Iron and Blood Cross Order, using his criminal network and business holdings to advance the organization''s interests in Trier. Cunning and intellectually sharp, he favors elaborate tests and psychological games over brute force when evaluating recruits — he dispatched Lumian Lee alongside Christo and Simon on a retrieval mission into Underground Trier, then set Lumian alone in a gutted building overnight, before formally embracing him as a brother and inducting him into the Order. He rewarded proven loyalty with Beyonder characteristics, including a Lucky One characteristic gifted to Lumian after the latter eliminated a Werewolf probing the Mob''s leadership. He maintained a romantic association with Franca Roland, who knew him as calculating and always several moves ahead. Gardner Martin died when the backlash from a Pride Armor claimed him.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Gardner Martin', 'Lumian Lee', 'Franca Roland', 'Philip', 'Olson', 'Christo', 'Simon'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'red-priest-pathway', 'iron-and-blood-cross-order', 'savoie-mob', 'sequence-5', 'reaper', 'intis-republic', 'criminal-organization', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 247),
  ('npc-olson', 'Olson — Reaper of the Iron and Blood Cross Order', 'npc', 'Olson is a deceased male Beyonder of the Red Priest pathway, having attained Sequence 5 — Reaper. During his life he served the Iron and Blood Cross Order as Supervisor of Trier''s Quartier 13, the city''s market district, exercising authority over Order operations there. A man over 1.8 metres tall, he had short auburn hair, reddish-brown eyes, thick eyebrows, and a wild beard, with a frame so lean he resembled a starved bear despite his imposing height. In his role as Supervisor, Olson delivered cryptic operational guidance to Order agents passing through his jurisdiction. He issued a three-part warning to Lumian Lee: what the eyes see may not be true; they will inevitably enter the Fourth Epoch''s Trier; and one should never readily trust the words of others. He was eventually killed by fellow Order member Gardner Martin, who decapitated him.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Olson', 'Gardner Martin', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'red-priest-pathway', 'iron-and-blood-cross-order', 'sequence-5', 'reaper', 'supervisor', 'quartier-13', 'market-district', 'deceased', 'spoiler', 'intis-republic'], 184),
  ('npc-bakerland-jean-madan', 'Bakerland Jean Madan — Intis Ambassador and Sequence 6 Conspirer', 'npc', 'Bakerland Jean Madan is the Intis Republic''s ambassador to the Loen Kingdom, stationed in Backlund, and simultaneously serves as chief of Intis intelligence operations on Loen soil. A Sequence 6 Beyonder of the Red Priest Pathway — bearing the title Conspirer — he is a skilled schemer who exploits his diplomatic cover to run destabilisation campaigns: covertly funding bloodshed, engineering incidents to inflame tensions between the nobility and the rich, and spreading seditious rumours to turn the public against the Loen government. Despite MI9 being unable to gather evidence of his crimes, his operations continue unchecked. In Backlund he directs the Zmanger gang, dispatching the operative Meursault to pursue Ian Wright over manuscripts tied to a third-generation difference machine, and later sending the assassin Rosago after the detective Sherlock Moriarty once the exposure of his Zmanger gang links prompts retaliation. This overreach triggers a Tarot Club assassination contract: Klein Moretti issues the mission, Miss Justice accepts and lets Fors Wall and Xio Derecha hire Mr. A to execute it. Bakerland is killed before he can act further, his diplomatic career and clandestine network cut short.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Bakerland Jean Madan', 'Meursault', 'Ian Wright', 'Rosago', 'Mr. A', 'Klein Moretti', 'Audrey Hall', 'Fors Wall', 'Xio Derecha'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['backlund', 'red-priest-pathway', 'intis-republic', 'intis-embassy', 'intelligence', 'ambassador', 'conspirer', 'zmanger-gang', 'tarot-club', 'deceased', 'spoiler', 'book-one'], 241),
  ('npc-margot', 'Margot — Provoker of the Poison Spur Mob', 'npc', 'Margot, alias Wolf, was a Sequence 8 Provoker of the Red Priest Pathway and a leader within the Poison Spur Mob operating in Trier. A thin man with closely cropped yellow hair, single-lidded blue eyes, a prominent nose bridge, thin lips, and faint scars on his face, he ran a predatory racket in the city''s market district: luring women newly arrived in Trier, swindling them dry, then forcing them into prostitution. He reported to Roger — the Poison Spur Mob''s boss — and commanded thugs who collected money from establishments such as the Auberge du Coq Doré. When Lumian Lee was seeking a target for the Fallen Mercury ability, Charlie Collent named Margot as someone deserving death. Lumian subsequently confronted Margot at his apartment on Rue du Rossignol and used Fallen Mercury to swap Margot''s fate with the fate of being attacked by the Montsouris ghost. Seeking protection, Margot turned to Roger, who performed a ritual to eliminate hidden threats — but Margot died mysteriously shortly after, the swapped fate proving irreversible.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Margot', 'Lumian Lee', 'Roger', 'Charlie Collent'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['trier', 'red-priest-pathway', 'poison-spur-mob', 'sequence-8', 'provoker', 'deceased', 'antagonist', 'criminal-underworld', 'spoiler'], 211),
  ('npc-meursault', 'Meursault — Zmanger Gang Enforcer and Red Priest Hunter', 'npc', 'Meursault was a highlander operating in Backlund during the early period of Klein Moretti''s career as the consulting detective Sherlock Holmes. Thin and weather-hardened, with deeply recessed gray-blue eyes and sun-darkened skin marking him as a man from the highland regions, he served as an executioner within the Zmanger gang — ranking near the top and almost equal to the gang''s own boss in authority and feared capability. As a Sequence 9 Hunter of the Red Priest Pathway, he possessed the foundational predatory instincts and tracking talents of that progression, going armed with a dow and small black-feathered arrows. Bakerland Jean Madan — the Intis Republic''s ambassador and intelligence chief in Loen — dispatched Meursault to locate Ian Wright, who had become entangled with manuscripts relating to third-generation difference machines. Meursault first made contact with Klein at the steam metro and later visited his rented apartment under the guise of hiring the detective to find Ian, only to be refused. That same evening Meursault returned and attacked Klein directly — and was killed by him. His death marked one of Klein''s earliest lethal confrontations in Backlund, establishing the stakes of the criminal underworld Klein was navigating.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Meursault', 'Bakerland Jean Madan', 'Ian Wright', 'Klein Moretti'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['backlund', 'red-priest-pathway', 'zmanger-gang', 'hunter-sequence', 'deceased', 'enforcer', 'highland', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 230),
  ('npc-poufer-sauron', 'Poufer Sauron — Beyonder of the Red Priest Pathway, Black Cat Circle', 'npc', 'Poufer Sauron is a middle-aged nobleman of the Sauron Family, resident of Quartier Éraste and Red Swan Castle in Trier. Though he inherited a considerable fortune, he spurned careers in politics, the military, and trade in favour of artistic life, working as a literary critic and a regular at the "Black Cat" salon gatherings. A mid-sequence practitioner of the Red Priest pathway, his refinement and casual charisma made him a natural centre of those literary circles. Gardner Martin dispatched Lumian Lee to infiltrate the Black Cat group by cultivating Poufer''s friendship, drawing Lumian into Trier''s hidden currents. During Black Cat gatherings Poufer proposed the game of King''s Pie. His fate was singular and grim: he ultimately fused with his ancestor Vermonda Sauron — a death that collapsed the boundary between descendant and the ancient power sleeping within the bloodline.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Poufer Sauron', 'Vermonda Sauron', 'Elros Einhorn', 'Gardner Martin', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[5], ARRAY['trier', 'red-priest-pathway', 'sauron-family', 'black-cat', 'literary-critic', 'intis-republic', 'mid-sequence', 'spoiler'], 192),
  ('npc-ait', 'Ait — "Hammer," Pugilist of the Poison Spur Mob', 'npc', 'Known by the street name "Hammer," Ait was a towering, broad-shouldered man — nearly 1.9 metres tall — who operated out of 25 Rue des Pavés in Trier''s Le Marché du Quartier du Gentleman district. Originally a promising member of the Savoie Mob, he was held in high regard by Baron Brignais, who planned to recommend him to the boss. Ait nonetheless betrayed the Savoie Mob and defected to the rival Poison Spur Mob, drawn by the prospect of faster access to Beyonder powers along the Twilight Giant Pathway. He achieved Sequence 8 — Pugilist — swiftly after the switch. A Pugilist''s fists carry the hardness and force of iron hammers; Ait was also adept with a revolver and a dirk, though he typically fought unarmed. Despite his imposing presence and Beyonder capability, he was inwardly a coward and would betray others'' secrets for even a small chance of survival. When Lumian Lee (operating as Ciel Dubois) was tasked by Brignais to assault a prominent Poison Spur figure, he targeted Ait, ambushed him in a washroom at the Salle de Gristmill, interrogated him, and killed him in 1358. Ait''s Pugilist Beyonder characteristic was subsequently sold to Gardner Martin for 18,000 verl d''or.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Ait', 'Lumian Lee', 'Baron Brignais', 'Gardner Martin'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['trier', 'twilight-giant-pathway', 'poison-spur-mob', 'savoie-mob', 'sequence-8', 'pugilist', 'intis-republic', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 238),
  ('npc-simon', 'Simon — "Giant" of the Savoie Mob, Trier', 'npc', 'Known as "Giant" Simon, this imposing Sequence 8 Pugilist of the Twilight Giant pathway operates as one of the Savoie Mob''s district leaders in Trier''s market quarter. Standing over 1.9 meters tall, powerfully built, and typically dressed in a figure-hugging black suit and wide-brimmed hat, Simon commands the domain of Rue du Rossignol — its dance halls and bars serve as his territory. He is a member of the Church of the God of Steam and Machinery. Within the mob, he holds a fractious rivalry with Baron Brignais, contesting control over the Salle de Bal Brise. Simon arms himself with a poison-coated dagger, bayonet, and boxing gloves — lacing each with Scorpion Poison — and carries an iron-gray pocket watch among his personal effects. When Lumian Lee ("Lion" Ciel) reveals a Mid-Sequence standing that outranks Simon''s own, the mob leader shamelessly declares Ciel his sworn elder brother, citing their Sequence difference as justification. Despite his crude humor, Simon is a practical combatant and a reliable underworld power in Trier''s criminal landscape.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Simon', 'Baron Brignais', 'Lumian Lee', 'Franca Roland'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['trier', 'twilight-giant-pathway', 'savoie-mob', 'pugilist', 'church-of-the-god-of-steam-and-machinery', 'underworld', 'sequence-8', 'intis-republic', 'spoiler'], 208),
  ('npc-sow', 'Sow — Port Pylos Patrol Pugilist', 'npc', 'Sow was a Sequence 8 Pugilist of the Twilight Giant pathway, stationed on Port Pylos''s patrol team in West Balam. A former adventurer who joined the patrol roughly a year before his death, he cut an imposing figure — dark brown skin, thick lips, over 1.8 meters tall — and carried a broadsword. Regarded as easygoing, if somewhat lazy and pleasure-seeking, he had covertly aligned himself with both Hisoka and the Rose School of Thought''s Indulgence Faction. Acting on Hisoka''s orders, Sow used a joker-faced poker card mystical item to force a Wraith possession upon patrol colleague Camus Castiya, then struck with his broadsword while Camus was trapped in illusion — an attempt to silence Camus and fellow member Kolobo. Camus broke free; Deputy Captain Reaza intervened, and Sow was killed by Reaza and Camus Castiya, his corpse torn apart by Reaza''s undead creatures. His death fell on the same day Lumian Lee advanced to Reaper. He worshipped the Mother Tree of Desire.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Sow', 'Hisoka', 'Camus Castiya', 'Reaza', 'Kolobo', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['balam', 'west-balam', 'port-pylos', 'twilight-giant-pathway', 'pugilist', 'patrol-team', 'rose-school-of-thought', 'indulgence-faction', 'mother-tree-of-desire', 'beyonder', 'sequence-8', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 244),
  ('npc-havre', 'Havre — Captain of the Mandated Punishers', 'npc', 'Havre was a captain within the Mandated Punishers, an enforcement division under the Church of the Lord of Storms in Tingen City. A Sequence 8 Beyonder of the Tyrant Pathway — known as a Folk of Rage — he maintained a working relationship with the Nighthawks and was a close friend of Old Neil, a former Nighthawk and clerk at the Blackthorn Security Company, with whom he shared drinks at the Hound Pub.

When a haunting at the docks targeted devotees of the Evernight Goddess, Havre met with Dunn Smith and handed jurisdiction to the Nighthawks. He then undertook a surveillance assignment: watching Megose and tracking Lanevus. During that operation, Havre lost control of his Beyonder characteristics and went rampant — at least Sequence 8 power, as Leonard Mitchell judged. The Nighthawks subdued the rampager; his identity was revealed only when a hip flask fell from the body. Old Neil, recognising his last friend, volunteered to take the killing shot before Leonard could fire.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Havre', 'Old Neil', 'Dunn Smith', 'Leonard Mitchell', 'Megose', 'Lanevus'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['tingen', 'tyrant-pathway', 'mandated-punishers', 'church-of-the-lord-of-storms', 'folk-of-rage', 'sequence-8', 'deceased', 'rampager', 'donghua-only', 'spoiler'], 246),
  ('npc-rhea', 'Rhea — Patrol Team Member, Folk of Rage', 'npc', 'Rhea is a Sequence 8 Beyonder of the Tyrant pathway, holding the grade of Folk of Rage, and serves as a member of the Patrol Team stationed in Tizamo Town, West Balam. Born into the Paca, a primitive tribe of Paz Valley in the Southern Continent, her life was shattered when the Loen Kingdom''s army attacked and scattered her people roughly a decade before the present day. Captured and sold multiple times, she eventually found herself in the Northern state. Seizing an opportunity, she escaped and sought refuge in Port Pylos, where the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun aided her. She credits that intervention as the turning point that pulled her from despair. She subsequently joined the Patrol Team, which gave her renewed purpose and stability. Armed with the Thunderclap Explosion ability, she carries out patrol duties alongside colleagues including the operative known as Louis Berry. Her tribal background and hard-won freedom lend her a fierce, self-reliant bearing, and her loyalty to both the Church and the Patrol Team reflects her gratitude for those who restored her dignity.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Rhea', 'Louis Berry'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['balam', 'west-balam', 'tizamo-town', 'tyrant-pathway', 'folk-of-rage', 'sequence-8', 'patrol-team', 'church-of-the-eternal-blazing-sun', 'southern-continent', 'paca-tribe', 'spoiler'], 232),
  ('npc-swain', 'Swain — Folk of Rage, Boss of the Evil Dragon Bar', 'npc', 'Swain is a Sequence 8 Folk of Rage on the Tyrant pathway and the proprietor of the Evil Dragon Bar, Tingen''s open-secret black market. A muscular older man who reeks of alcohol, he was once a captain of Tingen''s Mandated Punishers squad and is rumored to have served in the Royal Navy. He is an adherent of the Church of the Lord of Storms. Despite his disheveled, drink-sodden bearing, Swain retains the disciplined carriage of a veteran officer. He declined the chance to advance to Sequence 7 Seafarer, fearing that he would lose control of his Beyonder abilities — a rare act of self-aware restraint that has left him voluntarily stranded at Sequence 8. He counts Old Neil among his trusted associates. At his request, Klein Moretti and Old Neil assisted him in eliminating a Mandated Punisher who had lost control.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Swain', 'Old Neil', 'Klein Moretti'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['tingen', 'tyrant-pathway', 'folk-of-rage', 'sequence-8', 'mandated-punishers', 'evil-dragon-bar', 'church-of-the-lord-of-storms', 'loen-kingdom', 'black-market', 'spoiler'], 183),
  ('npc-susie', 'Susie — Dreamwalker Hound of the Visionary Pathway', 'npc', 'Susie is a golden retriever who accidentally consumed Audrey Hall''s Sequence 9 Spectator potion and became a fully cognizant Beyonder creature. She speaks Loenese, reads psychology texts, and advances along the Visionary Pathway without a human acting method, digesting potions with uncanny ease and no signs of losing control. Her intelligence and demeanor have grown with each advancement: she keeps a pair of gold-rimmed glasses hanging around her neck, cultivates an air of ladylike composure, and disarms expectations by reminding people she is, after all, just a dog.

In Backlund during Book 1, Susie served as Audrey''s loyal companion, discreetly observing social gatherings and watching doors from the vantage of a pet. She reached Sequence 5 Dreamwalker before departing the Hall estate with Audrey.

By the present era she operates in Trier as a practicing psychologist to Lumian Lee, having advanced to Sequence 4 Manipulator after Audrey herself reached Sequence 2 of the Visionary Pathway. Her work blends genuine therapeutic practice with the empathic and perception-altering abilities native to her pathway.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['Susie', 'Audrey Hall', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[4], ARRAY['trier', 'backlund', 'visionary-pathway', 'beyonder-creature', 'sequence-4', 'manipulator', 'psychology-alchemists', 'tarot-club', 'spoiler', 'golden-retriever', 'audrey-hall'], 221),
  ('npc-i-know-someone', 'I Know Someone — Hypnotist of April Fool''s', 'npc', 'Pierre Theuriau, known by his Research Society codename "I Know Someone," was a Sequence 6 Hypnotist of the Visionary pathway and a transmigrator from modern-era China. Based at Delta Asylum in Trier, Intis Republic, he operated as a psychiatrist while secretly serving the prank collective April Fool''s; he had previously been a member of the Curly-Haired Baboons Research Society. His obsession with mind manipulation had already cost him his sanity once; he regained consciousness to find himself interned at the very asylum he would later exploit as a cover. In Trier he covertly propagated the practice of lobotomy — causing numerous unnecessary deaths — and spread false medical folklore about human blood bread and mandrake root, framing these as revelations from the Celestial Worthy. As psychiatrist to Aurore Lee (codename Muggle), he deliberately worsened her condition across successive sessions, guiding the resurging personality of Roche Louise Sanson and betraying her private vulnerabilities to April Fool''s core members for amusement. After Lumian Lee apprehended him at Delta Asylum with the aid of Hidden Blade, Madam Magician, and Jenna, he was interrogated and then burned at the stake in the Rois Comprehensive Execution Ground, Prison District, Trier.', null, 5, 'trier', ARRAY['I Know Someone', 'Pierre Theuriau', 'Lumian Lee', 'Aurore Lee', 'Franca Roland', 'Loki', 'Mad Lady', 'Fors Wall'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['trier', 'visionary-pathway', 'april-fools', 'curly-haired-baboons-research-society', 'transmigrator', 'sequence-6', 'hypnotist', 'psychiatrist', 'delta-asylum', 'intis-republic', 'deceased', 'spoiler'], 253),
  ('npc-hilbert-alucard', 'Hilbert Alucard — Psychology Alchemists Examiner', 'npc', 'Hilbert Alucard is a Beyonder of the Visionary Pathway and a member of the Psychology Alchemists, a secret organization controlling that pathway''s formulas and based in the Garden of Eden — a city within the Sea of Collective Consciousness. A man of apparent Southern Continent descent in his forties, Alucard resides in Backlund, Loen Kingdom, where he works as a psychologist and jewelry designer, providing natural cover for his esoteric activities.

Within the Psychology Alchemists, Alucard holds an evaluative function: he subjected the candidate Audrey Hall to a telepathic examination before she was confirmed as an official member of the organization. His use of telepathic technique places him at mid-sequence on the Visionary Pathway; the wiki categorizes him as a Book One mid-sequence figure but leaves his exact rank blank — Sequence 7 (Psychiatrist) is the most supportable inference. He was introduced to Audrey alongside fellow member Escalante Oseleka by Lady Norma.

He presents as silent and reserved in demeanor. He is alive and active during the present era of play.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Hilbert Alucard', 'Audrey Hall', 'Escalante Oseleka', 'Lady Norma'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['backlund', 'visionary-pathway', 'psychology-alchemists', 'mid-sequence', 'examiner', 'psychologist', 'loen-kingdom', 'spoiler'], 228),
  ('npc-stephen-hampres', 'Stephen Hampres — Psychology Alchemists Seminar Convener, Backlund', 'npc', 'Stephen Hampres is a furniture merchant in Backlund, Loen Kingdom, and the convener of a covert psychological seminar run under an academic pretense by the Psychology Alchemists. In his thirties, he wears a gray tailcoat and a neatly trimmed mustache, and carries himself with the composed elegance of a university lecturer rather than a tradesman. Audrey Hall''s sharp observations reveal that his finances are worse than he presents, that he has many concerns and keeps his guard up, and that he uses facial products to maintain appearances. He is a low-sequence practitioner of the Visionary Pathway — sequence rank blank in available records, with Sequence 9 (Spectator) the most probable entry rank. Escalante Oseleka brought Audrey Hall to one of his gatherings, marking Audrey''s first encounter with the Psychology Alchemists. The organization itself operates under the influence of Hermes and functions as a division of the Twilight Hermit Order; Hampres''s own standing and intentions within it remain opaque.', null, 5, 'backlund', ARRAY['Stephen Hampres', 'Audrey Hall', 'Escalante Oseleka', 'Hvin Rambis', 'Pauli Derlau'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['backlund', 'visionary-pathway', 'psychology-alchemists', 'loen-kingdom', 'seminar-convener', 'low-sequence', 'twilight-hermit-order', 'spoiler'], 218),
  ('npc-kolobo', 'Kolobo — Patrol Team Beyonder of Port Pylos', 'npc', 'Kolobo is a Beyonder in his mid-twenties stationed with the Patrol Team in Port Pylos, West Balam. Dark-haired and azure-eyed, he operates at Sequence 8 on the Wheel of Fortune Pathway, bearing the designation of Robot. His pathway grants him sensitivity to Beyonder anomalies — he sensed the strangeness radiating from the entity known as Sow and reported it to his superiors, but to no avail. He followed fellow Patrol Team member Camus Castiya to Bram Andariel''s apartment to serve as a witness for the staged resolution of the serial-killer case, receiving a reward of five thousand verl d''or. Upon encountering the adventurer Louis Berry (Lumian Lee), Kolobo did not dare look directly at him, occasionally glimpsing large amounts of blood, flames, and death, and promptly warned Camus of the danger. He had also previously suppressed knowledge of Twanaku Tupián''s menace, fearing he would die if he spoke of it. Kolobo embodies the cautious, perceptive rank-and-file of Balam''s Beyonder civil order — capable of reading danger, yet constrained by institutional inertia and personal survival instinct.', null, 5, 'balam', ARRAY['Kolobo', 'Camus Castiya', 'Louis Berry (Lumian Lee)', 'Twanaku Tupián (Hisoka)', 'Bram Andariel', 'Sow'], ARRAY[8], ARRAY['balam', 'port-pylos', 'west-balam', 'wheel-of-fortune-pathway', 'patrol-team', 'sequence-8', 'robot', 'book-two', 'spoiler'], 218),
  ('npc-ademisaul', 'Ademisaul — Half-Monster of Tingen''s Underground Market', 'npc', 'Ademisaul is a pale, black-haired orphan living in the underground market of Tingen City, Loen Kingdom. Born a half-Monster on the Wheel of Fortune Pathway, he has always been able to see things others cannot, hear voices without source, and raves in fits he cannot control. Locals call him "Monster" — a nickname as much description as cruelty. When Klein Moretti encountered him at the market, Ademisaul mumbled that he smelled the scent of death the moment their eyes met, then collapsed with bleeding eyes — a sign of his distorted spiritual perception. He later dreamed of a field of corpses that included his own body, a premonition interpreted as a citywide-scale disaster. Despite that catastrophe nearly unfolding, Tingen survived, and Ademisaul was left very confused by events he sensed but could not comprehend. His name was preserved in the story of Tingen authored by the Sealed Artifact known as the Quill of Alzuhod.', null, 5, 'tingen', ARRAY['Ademisaul', 'Klein Moretti'], ARRAY[9], ARRAY['tingen', 'wheel-of-fortune-pathway', 'underground-market', 'loen-kingdom', 'orphan', 'half-beyonder', 'monster-sequence', 'spoiler'], 197),
  ('npc-berg', 'Berg — Detective of the Mandated Punishers', 'npc', 'Berg is a Sequence 7 White Tower Beyonder holding the Detective rank, active in Bayam as a member of the Mandated Punishers. He serves under Captain Cordoba Roye and is the team''s dedicated clue-finder, employing supernatural perception to reconstruct the truth of criminal events. Affiliated with the Church of the Lord of Storms, the Mandated Punishers are a division of Beyonders under that Church — addressing supernatural issues among its believers, with most members following the Tyrant Pathway. Berg is unusual within the team as its White Tower representative, providing the analytical and investigative function his sequence enables. His Detective abilities grant preternatural insight into crime scenes, tracing evidence beyond mundane means. Berg appears in Book One during the Beyonder affairs surrounding Bayam, operating as a living operative allied with Cordoba Roye and embodying the mid-sequence strength of the White Tower pathway in service of the Church''s investigative arm.', null, 5, 'bayam', ARRAY['Berg', 'Cordoba Roye'], ARRAY[7], ARRAY['bayam', 'white-tower-pathway', 'mandated-punishers', 'church-of-the-lord-of-storms', 'detective', 'sequence-7', 'book-one', 'spoiler'], 198),
  ('npc-basil', 'Basil — Bone Splitter, Most Trusted Subordinate of Admiral Deep Sea', 'npc', 'Known by the epithet Bone Splitter, Basil is a pirate captain and the most trusted subordinate of Howl Constantine, the feared Admiral Deep Sea. He commands the Black Octopus, a stealth submersible recovered from the ruins of a sunken city by Constantine — one of two such relics the Admiral retrieved alongside his own flagship, the Newins. Basil carries a bounty of 250,000 verl d''or, a sum that far exceeds most non-Admiral pirates and marks him as a serious threat in the sea lanes. He is known for cold-blooded brutality and takes evident pleasure in torturing captives. Lumian Lee, traveling under the alias Louis Berry, encountered the Black Octopus in the waters off Port Santa in the Feynapotter Kingdom; Basil chose to retreat without engaging after apparently sensing the combined threat of the Beyonders aboard the merchant vessel Flying Bird. Lumian assessed that Basil likely holds the Danger Premonition ability characteristic of a Sequence 6 Devil on the Abyss pathway — the instinct that drove him away. His current whereabouts remain unknown; he may be encountered again along the Feynapotter coast or wider sea routes.', null, 5, 'feysac', ARRAY['Basil', 'Howl Constantine', 'Lumian Lee'], ARRAY[6], ARRAY['feysac', 'abyss-pathway', 'pirate', 'black-octopus', 'book-two', 'spoiler', 'sea-lanes', 'feynapotter'], 240),
  ('npc-tirie', 'Tirié — Abomination of the Chained Pathway', 'npc', 'Tirié is a Sequence 1 Abomination of the Chained Pathway and an angel of the Rose School of Thought. She was born in Year 1359 of the Fifth Epoch inside Project Vortex, created from the Mother Goddess of Depravity''s corruption of the Chained God. This corruption originated with Roselle Gustav and was transferred through transactions between the indulgence faction of the Rose School of Thought and the Nightstalkers. Her birth caused the Chained God''s final Sequence 1 Abomination Beyonder characteristic to be peeled away from him. In true form she is tall and enormous, humanoid yet like grotesque trees, covered in pitch-black viscous tar-like liquid, with numerous bizarre and sickening arms bearing bulging crimson eyeballs with prominent blood vessels, pale embedded skull heads, or tongues covered in sharp teeth. Her appearance mirrors that of her brother Suah, also a Sequence 1 Abomination. She is affiliated with the Rose School of Thought and the Bliss Society, and venerates the Mother Tree of Desire. Late in the Fifth Epoch, Tirié and Suah appeared together at the bottom of Underground Trier and merged with the miraculously healed Tree of Shadow, allowing it to grow massively. She died at the end of July 1360 of the Fifth Epoch.', 'chained', 5, null, ARRAY['Chained God', 'Mother Goddess of Depravity', 'Suah', 'Roselle Gustav'], ARRAY[1], ARRAY['chained-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'rose-school-of-thought', 'bliss-society', 'mother-tree-of-desire', 'project-vortex', 'underground-trier', 'tree-of-shadow', 'abomination', 'sequence-1', 'book-two'], 213),
  ('npc-marianne', 'Marianne — Servant of Concealment', 'npc', 'Marianne was the Pope of the Church of the Evernight Goddess during the Fourth Epoch, placing her among the highest mortal — and beyond-mortal — authorities of the darkness pathway. As a Sequence 2 Servant of Concealment, she stood at the Angel tier of the pathway capped by the Evernight Goddess herself.

She perished during the War of the Four Emperors, dying inside Fourth Epoch Trier. Her death during that cataclysmic conflict reflects the scale of destruction that closed the epoch. Afterward, the Church of the Evernight Goddess retrieved her Beyonder characteristics, preserving the Servant of Concealment Sequence 2 ingredient rather than allowing it to be lost or claimed by rival factions.

Narrators should treat Marianne as a historical figure of the deep past — a confirmed Sequence 2 Angel whose characteristics were reclaimed by the Church, meaning that Sequence slot potentially fed the lineage of subsequent darkness pathway Angels. Her role as Pope underscores that the Church of the Evernight Goddess has long integrated its highest clergy with its highest-sequence Beyonders.', 'darkness', 4, null, ARRAY['Marianne'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['darkness-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'fourth-epoch', 'war-of-the-four-emperors', 'historical', 'pope'], 223),
  ('npc-lius', 'Lius — Death Consul', 'npc', 'Lius was a Sequence 2 Death Consul of the Death pathway and a Blessed of ancient Death — the deity Salinger — active in the Fourth Epoch. He was affiliated with the Church of Death.

Lius perished during the War of the Four Emperors, dying inside Fourth Epoch Trier (the underground city). His Beyonder characteristics were retrieved by the Church of Death after he fell, preventing them from scattering or being claimed by enemies.

Beyond his death and the recovery of his characteristics, no detailed deeds or motivations are recorded. His existence confirms that the Death pathway had at least one active Sequence 2 operative during the Fourth Epoch, and that the Church of Death maintained continuity of its highest-tier resources through the war''s catastrophic losses. Narrator note: Lius is mentioned only in passing (Book 2, Chapter 349) and has no expanded dialogue or scene presence — treat him as historical context, not an active character.', 'death', 4, null, ARRAY['Salinger'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['death-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'church-of-death', 'fourth-epoch', 'war-of-the-four-emperors', 'historical'], 236),
  ('npc-demoness-of-blue', 'Demoness of Blue — Catastrophe', 'npc', 'The Demoness of Blue is one of four Sequence 2 Angels — a Catastrophe of the Demoness Pathway — that the Demoness Sect possessed as of 1359 of the Fifth Epoch, as attested by Fors Wall (Madam Magician). Her true name is unknown; the alias "Demoness of Blue" is the only identifier on record. She was formerly male before ascending through the Demoness Pathway, which reshapes its adherents toward the Primordial Demoness''s image. A Catastrophe is a being of overwhelming destructive potential, second only to the pathway''s Sequence 1, the Apocalypse.

She perished during the Day of Many Disasters, the catastrophic supernatural event that killed numerous powerful beings across the Fifth Epoch. Her Beyonder characteristics did not dissipate: they condensed into the Grade 0 Sealed Artifact known as the Calamity of Crimson, a potent and dangerous relic born directly from a Catastrophe-level essence. As of the novel''s main timeline she is dead; her legacy persists entirely through that Sealed Artifact.

Narrator note: The Calamity of Crimson is a Grade 0 Sealed Artifact — the most powerful artifact tier — with power equivalent to a Sequence 2 Catastrophe. Player characters who encounter or seek this artifact are dealing with residual power at the highest relic threshold in the setting.', 'demoness', 5, null, ARRAY['Fors Wall', 'Judith'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['demoness-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'demoness-sect', 'sealed-artifact', 'catastrophe', 'day-of-many-disasters', 'calamity-of-crimson'], 220),
  ('npc-demoness-of-purple', 'Demoness of Purple — Catastrophe Angel of the Demoness Sect', 'npc', 'The Demoness of Purple is a Sequence 2 Catastrophe of the Demoness Pathway and one of the four Angels serving the Demoness Sect as of 1359 of the Fifth Epoch. Their true name is unknown; they were formerly male before ascending through the Demoness Pathway and its characteristic transformation into a mythical creature form.

Within the Demoness Sect''s hierarchy, the Demoness of Purple operated under the Matriarch Judith. As one of only four Sequence 2 Angels the Demoness Sect maintained, they represented a rare and formidable tier of beyonder power — Catastrophe-ranked entities capable of acts that reshape local reality.

The Demoness of Purple perished during The Day of Many Disasters, one of the pivotal catastrophic events of the Fifth Epoch. Following their death, their Beyonder Characteristics were obtained by Ouroboros. This loss reduced the sect''s Angel count and represented a significant transfer of accumulated Catastrophe-level power.

Narrator note: The Demoness of Purple is a background figure mentioned in a single reference (Book 2, Ch. 889). No personal history, abilities beyond their sequence tier, or individual feats are established in canon. Do not invent specifics beyond what is noted here.', 'demoness', 5, null, ARRAY['Judith', 'Ouroboros', 'Fors Wall'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['demoness-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'demoness-sect', 'catastrophe', 'day-of-many-disasters'], 212),
  ('npc-tissavica', 'Tissavica — Demoness of Yellow', 'npc', 'Tissavica, known as the **Demoness of Yellow**, is a Sequence 2 Catastrophe Angel of the Demoness Sect, one of four such Angels the sect maintained as of 1359 of the Fifth Epoch.

Formerly male before ascending the Demoness Pathway, Tissavica now presents as a woman in a yellow frilled dress with a playful bonnet and a sly smile.

She serves under **Judith**, a higher-ranked figure in the Demoness Sect hierarchy, and her religious devotion is directed toward the **Primordial Demoness**, the god anchoring the pathway.

As one of the Demoness Sect''s four Sequence 2 Angels, Tissavica is a significant pillar of the organization''s operational capability — a Catastrophe-rank figure any sufficiently informed character would treat with extreme caution.

She is surfaced through **Fors Wall**''s intelligence as Madam Magician, placing Tissavica''s existence within known Beyonder circles of the Fifth Epoch.

**Narrator note:** Tissavica has minimal on-page presence; treat her as an identified power rather than a developed character. Her existence confirms the Demoness Sect has multilayer Angel-tier depth.', 'demoness', 5, null, ARRAY['Tissavica', 'Judith', 'Fors Wall'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['demoness-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'demoness-sect', 'catastrophe', 'sequence-2', 'primordial-demoness'], 200),
  ('npc-mirror-roselle-gustav', 'Mirror Roselle Gustav — Knowledge Emperor', 'npc', 'Mirror Roselle Gustav is the mirror-world counterpart of Roselle Gustav and the undisputed leader of the Mirror People, the civilisation that inhabits the reflective dimension. She presents as a voluptuous woman with chestnut hair, blue eyes, and a mature, commanding presence, dressed in a black dress beneath a jewel-inlaid golden crown — hence her alias, Empress Roselle.

She stands at Sequence 1 of the Hermit Pathway, bearing the title Knowledge Emperor, one step below the True God rank (Sequence 0, Hermit). Her infobox records prior progression along the Paragon Pathway from Sequence 9 through 2, suggesting unusually broad mastery of Beyonder characteristics before consolidating on the Hermit Pathway.

During Book Two she operates as a pragmatic power broker, forming temporary alliances with the Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings, Zaratul, and Adam, while maintaining steadier ties to Pualis de Roquefort and her blood-kin descendant Louis Gustav. Her family connections mirror those of the original Roselle: Bernadette Gustav is her eldest daughter, the deceased Ciel Gustav was her eldest son, and Bornova Gustav is her second son.

For the narrator, Mirror Roselle Gustav represents a cryptic, high-agency Angel whose loyalties track her own agenda as sovereign of the Mirror People rather than any established Outer Deity or secret organisation.', 'hermit', 5, null, ARRAY['Mirror Roselle Gustav', 'Roselle Gustav', 'Zaratul', 'Adam', 'Pualis de Roquefort', 'Louis Gustav', 'Bernadette Gustav', 'Ciel Gustav', 'Bornova Gustav', 'Celestial Worthy of Heaven and Earth for Blessings'], ARRAY[1], ARRAY['hermit-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'mirror-people', 'knowledge-emperor', 'book-two', 'paragon-pathway', 'intis-republic', 'trier', 'roselle-family'], 228),
  ('npc-zedus', 'Zedus — the Life-Giver', 'npc', 'Zedus is a Sequence 2 Life-Giver on the Moon Pathway and a Boon Recipient bound to Lumian Lee. Born in the mid-First Epoch from the union of Primordial God Almighty and the sentient Brood Hive, Zedus and his elder twin sister Omebella were Mythical Creatures of the Moon and Mother Pathways respectively. Slain by Omebella in the First Epoch, his dismembered body was scattered; from the start of the Fifth Epoch his severed hand became a Spirit World legend known as the Abscessed Hand — an oversized, decaying hand that left trails of lifeless bodies.

When Lumian Lee reached Sequence 7 (Contractee), he contracted the Abscessed Hand on the condition that he locate all of Zedus''s remaining body parts. After a search across Morora and the Underworld, Lumian reunited the fragments and triggered Zedus''s physical resurrection. Zedus briefly fell under puppet-control of artifact 0-01 and expressed bone-deep hatred toward Omebella rather than gratitude.

During the Apocalypse, under Lumian''s command within Sefirah Castle, Zedus called out "Mother" to reinforce the symbolism of the Mother Goddess of Depravity, enabling Lumian to destroy the Gift of the Land and Lilith — symbolically severing Omebella''s link between the Mother Goddess and the Brood Hive. After rebirth his lineage shifted to Mother Goddess of Depravity (Divine Mother) and the deceased Eternal Blazing Sun (Divine Father). He now resides in Lumian Lee''s Divine Kingdom within the Mirror World.', 'moon', 5, null, ARRAY['Lumian Lee', 'Omebella', 'Primordial God Almighty', 'Brood Hive', 'Mother Goddess of Depravity', 'Eternal Blazing Sun', 'Fors Wall', 'Albus Medici', 'Julie'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['moon-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'life-giver', 'boon-recipient', 'mythical-creature', 'first-epoch', 'mirror-world', 'morora', 'sefirah-castle', 'apocalypse', 'spirit-world', 'twin-siblings'], 230),
  ('npc-pualis-de-roquefort', 'Pualis de Roquefort — Beauty Goddess', 'npc', 'Pualis de Roquefort, codenamed Madame Night, is a member of the Nightstalkers and a devoted follower of the Mother Goddess of Depravity. Originally born male as Pulitt de Roquefort — a dandy of Trier with noble but title-stripped ancestry — she changed sex upon advancing to Sequence 5 (Banshee) of the Chaos Primogenitor Pathway.

At the outset of Book Two, Pualis posed as the wife of Administrator Béost in Cordu Village, working to establish a Paramita and recruit believers for the Great Mother. She seduced Guillaume Bénet and bore a child by him — a child Guillaume later killed, unaware it was his. Expelled from Cordu after a combined assault by Guillaume, Louis Lund, and Aurore Lee, she retained an intense, unrequited obsession with Aurore throughout the story.

She participated in the Hostel ritual that opened the door to Fourth Epoch Trier, and later entered the Dream City (the Fool''s Dream) on behalf of the Great Mother, aiming to eliminate any chance for the Celestial Worthy to reverse the situation.

After The Day of Many Disasters, the Great Mother temporarily elevated her to Sequence 1 — Beauty Goddess (Moon Pathway). She then returned to the Great Mother''s embrace to accommodate the Brood Hive, dying in that act; her scarlet eyes shone like miniatures of the crimson moon.

As a Boon Recipient she also held Chaos Primogenitor Sequence 4 (Madame). Family: husband Béost, daughter Omebella, and son Zedus.', 'moon', 5, null, ARRAY['Béost', 'Guillaume Bénet', 'Omebella', 'Zedus', 'Aurore Lee', 'Lumian Lee', 'Mother Goddess of Depravity'], ARRAY[1], ARRAY['moon-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'nightstalkers', 'chaos-primogenitor-pathway', 'boon-recipient', 'book-two', 'intis-republic', 'cordu-village', 'trier', 'great-mother'], 237),
  ('npc-snarner-einhorn', 'Snarner Einhorn — The Embodiment of Iron and Blood', 'npc', 'Snarner Einhorn is a Sequence 2 Weather Warlock of the Red Priest Pathway and a member of the Einhorn Family, one of Feysac''s great noble houses. Standing over 1.8 meters tall with long dark-red hair, flamboyant golden earrings, and androgynous, handsome features, Snarner is nonetheless battle-hardened beneath that striking exterior.

Snarner bears four honorific names: The Embodiment of Iron and Blood; The Symbol of the Calamity of War; The Priest who controls the Weather; The Great Snarner Einhorn.

At the Angel tier of the Red Priest Pathway, Snarner commands weather on a battlefield scale. When Elros Einhorn summoned Snarner at Red Swan Castle after the door to Fourth Epoch Trier had briefly opened, Snarner joined the fight against Vermonda Sauron inside that temporal pocket. The engagement ended in a tactical retreat when the Red Angel Evil Spirit Medici — a Sequence 1 Conqueror of the same pathway — entered the fray.

Narrators should note Snarner''s loyalty to Einhorn Family interests: Snarner''s first words upon arrival concerned reclaiming the family''s most important object lost in a prior war, signaling that Snarner treats every battle as an opportunity to restore dynastic power.', 'red-priest', 5, null, ARRAY['Snarner Einhorn', 'Elros Einhorn', 'Vermonda Sauron', 'Sauron-Einhorn-Medici'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['red-priest-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'einhorn-family', 'feysac-empire', 'weather-warlock', 'sequence-2', 'book-two'], 247),
  ('npc-lutique', 'Lutique — White Angel of the Eternal Blazing Sun', 'npc', 'Lutique, known by the honorific Saint Lutique, is a male Sequence 1 White Angel of the Sun pathway and a member of the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun.

Originally a senior Sequence 2 Lightseeker, Lutique''s ascent to Sequence 1 came through extraordinary circumstance. When the Eternal Blazing Sun — the deity who once anchored the Sun pathway — perished during The Day of Many Disasters, Klein Moretti (The Fool) recovered and returned the Sequence 1 Beyonder characteristics that had been left without a proper successor. Lutique received these characteristics and successfully advanced to White Angel.

Having reached the highest angel tier of the Sun pathway, Lutique exists as a complete Mythical Creature, having transcended his former human form. He counts The Fool among his allies and directs his enmity toward believers of the Outer Deities. He remains affiliated with the Church of the Eternal Blazing Sun.', 'sun', 5, null, ARRAY['Klein Moretti', 'Eternal Blazing Sun'], ARRAY[1], ARRAY['sun-pathway', 'angel', 'white-angel', 'sequence-1', 'church-of-the-eternal-blazing-sun', 'spoiler', 'mythical-creature', 'book-two', 'day-of-many-disasters'], 183),
  ('npc-dabomachie', 'Dabomachie — Hand of God', 'npc', 'Dabomachie is the current Pope of the Church of the Evernight Goddess and one of the most senior clerical figures of the Goddess of Evernight''s faith on the continent. An elderly man with white hair, beard, and serene countenance, he is a Switched Pathways Beyonder who walked the Darkness pathway from Sequence 9 all the way to Sequence 2 before transferring to the Twilight Giant pathway. In the month leading up to The Apocalypse he advanced to Sequence 1: Hand of God of the Twilight Giant pathway. Prior to the Death of the Primordial Demoness, Leonard Mitchell met Dabomachie at the Cathedral of Serenity — the Church of the Evernight Goddess headquarters — to petition for temporary use of Sealed Artifact 0-17, the Angel of Concealment. Dabomachie could not personally participate in that operation, as too many Angels concentrating in the World of Ruins at one time would weaken the protected zones'' defenses and risk inviting the danger of the Great Mother. During The Apocalypse itself he fought alongside the Angels from Earth against the invading Angels of the Outer Deities, standing as one of humanity''s ultimate bulwarks. His title within the Church is Saint Dabomachie.', 'twilight-giant', 5, null, ARRAY['Dabomachie', 'Leonard Mitchell'], ARRAY[1], ARRAY['twilight-giant-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'church-of-the-evernight-goddess', 'darkness-pathway', 'switched-pathways', 'pope', 'apocalypse'], 205),
  ('npc-edefana', 'Edefana — Discerner of the Visionary Pathway', 'npc', 'Edefana is an ancient mind dragon and a Sequence 2 Discerner of the Visionary Pathway — the second-highest rank an Angel of that pathway can hold. Born in the First Epoch, he is one of three mind dragons who persisted through the Second Epoch into the Fifth Epoch, making him an extraordinarily rare living relic of earlier ages of the world. A grayish-white dragon bearing a lizard-like face showing unmistakable signs of age, his appearance reflects a lifespan exceeding seven thousand years. His most notable historical distinction is that he is the first officially known Angel to die of old age — a fact that underscores both the extreme longevity of high-sequence Beyonders and the limits even they eventually face. During the Fifth Epoch, Audrey Hall spent years pursuing Edefana. When Mr. Fool descended upon Trier, Edefana wove a dream for Audrey at that moment, then subsequently died of old age. Narrators should treat Edefana as a figure of melancholy grandeur — a being who outlasted almost every contemporary, yet whose eventual mortality carries thematic weight about the ceiling of Beyonder power and the passage of epochs.', 'visionary', 5, null, ARRAY['Audrey Hall', 'Klein Moretti'], ARRAY[2], ARRAY['visionary-pathway', 'angel', 'spoiler', 'dragon', 'mind-dragon', 'second-epoch-survivor', 'deceased'], 243)
on conflict (slug) do update set
  title = excluded.title,
  category = excluded.category,
  content = excluded.content,
  pathway = excluded.pathway,
  epoch = excluded.epoch,
  city = excluded.city,
  npcs = excluded.npcs,
  sequences = excluded.sequences,
  tags = excluded.tags,
  token_count = excluded.token_count;
